window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b024-043a7304b4160676.json"]={sha256:"043a7304b41606762810e01296a56b5ae7fff91870de5ff9c31a975c2d224bd9",value:{"id":"b024","title":"東京晴空塔","titleEn":"Tokyo Skytree","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從三角形基底到圓形頂部的塔身斷面與格構風力出發，理解心柱與鋼塔之間以油壓阻尼器耦合的減振機制，計算直徑 2.3 m 鋼管與節狀壁樁的容量，再處理日照彎曲下的施工測量、在中央豎井內頂升天線塔、阻尼器的雙線性特性驗證、2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查，最後是冬季落冰與鋼管塔的防蝕維護。","summaryEn":"Starting from the tower's triangle-to-circle section and the wind force on an open lattice, understand how the central column and steel tower are coupled through oil dampers to reduce vibration, compute the capacity of 2.3 m steel tubes and knuckle-wall piles, then handle construction surveys under solar bowing, lifting the antenna mast inside the central shaft, verifying bilinear damper behaviour, inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake, and finally falling ice and corrosion upkeep of a tubular steel tower.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-supertall","subcategoryTitle":"超高層建築巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"Supertall building landmarks","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-supertall","learningTags":["structures","st-supertall","tower"],"architectureFamily":"tower","architectureNodes":[["三角形鋼管桁架塔身","Triangular tubular steel truss"],["鋼筋混凝土心柱","Concrete central column"],["油壓阻尼器連接","Oil-damper connections"],["天線塔與頂部阻尼器","Antenna mast and top dampers"],["節狀壁樁基礎","Knuckle-wall pile foundations"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,2],[1,2],[3,0],[0,4],[1,4]],"diagram":{"type":"tower","labels":["三角形鋼管桁架塔身","鋼筋混凝土心柱","油壓阻尼器連接","天線塔與頂部阻尼器","節狀壁樁基礎"],"labelsEn":["Triangular tubular steel truss","Concrete central column","Oil-damper connections","Antenna mast and top dampers","Knuckle-wall pile foundations"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"三腳塔腳柱受力練習：底部為邊長 s = 68 m 的正三角形，三支腳柱到形心距 R = s/√3 ≈ 39.3 m。若風造成的傾覆彎矩 M = 3,000 MN·m 作用於平行某一邊的軸，對應頂點腳柱的軸力變化 F₁ = M/(1.5R) ≈ 3,000/58.9 ≈ 50.9 MN，另兩腳各 F₂ = M/(3R) ≈ 25.5 MN、方向相反。設總重 400 MN、每腳 133.3 MN：頂點腳柱減壓後剩 133.3 − 50.9 ≈ 82.4 MN，另兩腳增為約 158.8 MN；風向反轉時頂點腳約 184.3 MN、另兩腳約 107.9 MN。若地震垂直加速度使重力暫時減少 30%，頂點腳只剩 0.7×133.3 − 50.9 ≈ 42.4 MN。若底邊縮為 50 m，R ≈ 28.9 m、F₁ ≈ 69.3 MN，頂點腳剩約 64.1 MN，餘裕明顯縮小。由此可見基底寬度與節狀壁樁的拉拔能力為何同樣重要。數值為教學假設，不代表東京晴空塔的設計值。","textEn":"Tripod leg forces: the base is an equilateral triangle with side s = 68 m, so each leg is R = s/√3 ≈ 39.3 m from the centroid. An overturning moment M = 3,000 MN·m about an axis parallel to one side changes the apex leg force by F₁ = M/(1.5R) ≈ 3,000/58.9 ≈ 50.9 MN and the other two legs by F₂ = M/(3R) ≈ 25.5 MN each in the opposite sense. With a total weight of 400 MN, 133.3 MN per leg, the apex leg drops to 133.3 − 50.9 ≈ 82.4 MN while the other two rise to about 158.8 MN; with the wind reversed the apex leg carries about 184.3 MN and the others about 107.9 MN. If vertical earthquake acceleration briefly reduces gravity by 30%, the apex leg keeps only 0.7×133.3 − 50.9 ≈ 42.4 MN. With a 50 m base side, R ≈ 28.9 m and F₁ ≈ 69.3 MN, leaving the apex leg about 64.1 MN, a clearly reduced margin. This is why base width and the uplift capacity of the knuckle wall piles matter equally. Values are teaching assumptions, not Tokyo Skytree's design values.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b024-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「三角形基底、圓形頂部與格構風力」與「心柱與鋼塔的相位差減振」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Triangular base, circular top and wind on a lattice\" and \"Out-of-phase damping between central column and tower\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b024-v13-01","title":"三角形基底、圓形頂部與格構風力：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Triangular base, circular top and wind on a lattice: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「三角形到圓形的斷面」如何影響東京晴空塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Triangle-to-circle section” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tokyo Skytree”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"東京晴空塔底部是邊長約 68 m 的正三角形，三支腳柱向上逐漸收攏，斷面由三角形轉為圓形，約在 350 m 以上成為圓筒狀；高度與底寬比約 9：1，是極為細長的獨立塔。三角形基底在狹窄基地內提供最大的力臂與穩定性，圓形上部則讓不同風向的阻力較一致。塔身是鋼管桁架而非實心外牆，風力取決於桿件的投影面積與實積率，而不是整個輪廓面積。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「三角形到圓形的斷面」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Tokyo Skytree stands on an equilateral triangle with sides of about 68 m; its three legs draw together as they rise, so the section changes from a triangle to a circle and becomes cylindrical above about 350 m. Its height-to-base ratio is about 9 to 1, making it an extremely slender free-standing tower. The triangular base gives the largest lever arm and stability on a narrow site, while the circular upper section makes drag more uniform across wind directions. The body is a tubular steel truss rather than a solid skin, so wind force depends on member projected area and solidity ratio rather than on the whole outline. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Triangle-to-circle section” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：格構塔單位高度風力 F = q·C_f·φ·B。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Wind force per unit height on a lattice tower F = q·C_f·φ·B.","failure":"常見誤解：「格構塔透風，所以風力可以忽略。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A lattice tower lets the wind through, so wind force can be ignored.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「三角形到圓形的斷面」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Triangle-to-circle section”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-01-k1","title":"三角形基底、圓形頂部與格構風力","titleEn":"Triangular base, circular top and wind on a lattice","text":"東京晴空塔底部是邊長約 68 m 的正三角形，三支腳柱向上逐漸收攏，斷面由三角形轉為圓形，約在 350 m 以上成為圓筒狀；高度與底寬比約 9：1，是極為細長的獨立塔。三角形基底在狹窄基地內提供最大的力臂與穩定性，圓形上部則讓不同風向的阻力較一致。","textEn":"Tokyo Skytree stands on an equilateral triangle with sides of about 68 m; its three legs draw together as they rise, so the section changes from a triangle to a circle and becomes cylindrical above about 350 m. Its height-to-base ratio is about 9 to 1, making it an extremely slender free-standing tower.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：格構塔透風，所以風力可以忽略。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A lattice tower lets the wind through, so wind force can be ignored. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「三角形基底、圓形頂部與格構風力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Triangular base, circular top and wind on a lattice\" is correct?","options":["格構塔透風，所以風力可以忽略。","東京晴空塔底部是邊長約 68 m 的正三角形，三支腳柱向上逐漸收攏，斷面由三角形轉為圓形，約在 350 m 以上成為圓筒狀。","心柱是用來支撐鋼塔重量的主柱。"],"optionsEn":["A lattice tower lets the wind through, so wind force can be ignored.","Tokyo Skytree stands on an equilateral triangle with sides of about 68 m.","The central column is the main column that carries the steel tower's weight."],"answer":1,"explanation":"東京晴空塔底部是邊長約 68 m 的正三角形，三支腳柱向上逐漸收攏，斷面由三角形轉為圓形，約在 350 m 以上成為圓筒狀；高度與底寬比約 9：1，是極為細長的獨立塔。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Tokyo Skytree stands on an equilateral triangle with sides of about 68 m; its three legs draw together as they rise, so the section changes from a triangle to a circle and becomes cylindrical above about 350 m. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b024-v13-02","title":"三角形基底、圓形頂部與格構風力：定量估算","titleEn":"Triangular base, circular top and wind on a lattice: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「三角形到圓形的斷面」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Triangle-to-circle section” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：格構塔單位高度風力 F = q·C_f·φ·B。風速 40 m/s 時 q = ½×1.225×40² ≈ 980 Pa；取 C_f = 2.0、實積率 φ = 0.25、外輪廓寬 B = 40 m，F = 980×2.0×0.25×40 ≈ 19.6 kN/m；若沿 600 m 均布，基底彎矩約 19.6×600²/2 ≈ 3.5 GN·m。細長比 634/68 ≈ 9.3。風速與係數為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Wind force per unit height on a lattice tower F = q·C_f·φ·B. At 40 m/s, q = ½×1.225×40² ≈ 980 Pa; with C_f = 2.0, solidity φ = 0.25 and outline width B = 40 m, F = 980×2.0×0.25×40 ≈ 19.6 kN/m, and spread over 600 m the base moment is about 19.6×600²/2 ≈ 3.5 GN·m. The slenderness is 634/68 ≈ 9.3. Wind speed and coefficients are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以風洞試驗量測不同高度斷面的阻力係數與實積率影響，並確認圓形段沒有明顯的渦流共振；分析模型要逐段輸入桿件投影面積，與風洞結果比較基底剪力與彎矩，並檢查天線、維修平台等附掛物增加的受風面積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure drag coefficients and solidity effects for sections at different heights in the wind tunnel and confirm that the circular segment shows no marked vortex resonance; enter member projected areas segment by segment in the analysis model, compare base shear and moment with the wind-tunnel results, and account for added area from antennas and maintenance platforms.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"格構塔單位高度風力 F = q·C_f·φ·B。風速 40 m/s 時 q = ½×1.225×40² ≈ 980 Pa；取 C_f = 2.0、實積率 φ = 0.25、外輪廓寬 B = 40 m，F = 980×2.0×0.25×40 ≈ 19.6 kN/m；若沿 600 m 均布，基底彎矩約 19.6×600²/2 ≈ 3.5 GN·m。細長比 634/68 ≈ 9.3。風速與係數為教學假設。","textEn":"Wind force per unit height on a lattice tower F = q·C_f·φ·B. At 40 m/s, q = ½×1.225×40² ≈ 980 Pa; with C_f = 2.0, solidity φ = 0.25 and outline width B = 40 m, F = 980×2.0×0.25×40 ≈ 19.6 kN/m, and spread over 600 m the base moment is about 19.6×600²/2 ≈ 3.5 GN·m. The slenderness is 634/68 ≈ 9.3. Wind speed and coefficients are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「三角形基底、圓形頂部與格構風力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Triangular base, circular top and wind on a lattice\", which statement holds?","options":["塔很重，所以基礎只需要考慮下壓，不會受拉。","在豎井內頂升比較安全，所以不需要另做結構分析。","格構塔單位高度風力 F = q·C_f·φ·B。"],"optionsEn":["The tower is heavy, so its foundation only needs to resist compression and never tension.","Lifting inside the shaft is safer, so no separate structural analysis is needed.","Wind force per unit height on a lattice tower F = q·C_f·φ·B."],"answer":2,"explanation":"格構塔單位高度風力 F = q·C_f·φ·B。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Wind force per unit height on a lattice tower F = q·C_f·φ·B. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b024-v13-03","title":"三角形基底、圓形頂部與格構風力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Triangular base, circular top and wind on a lattice: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「三角形到圓形的斷面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Triangle-to-circle section” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以風洞試驗量測不同高度斷面的阻力係數與實積率影響，並確認圓形段沒有明顯的渦流共振；分析模型要逐段輸入桿件投影面積，與風洞結果比較基底剪力與彎矩，並檢查天線、維修平台等附掛物增加的受風面積。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure drag coefficients and solidity effects for sections at different heights in the wind tunnel and confirm that the circular segment shows no marked vortex resonance; enter member projected areas segment by segment in the analysis model, compare base shear and moment with the wind-tunnel results, and account for added area from antennas and maintenance platforms. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立附掛物登錄制度：任何新增天線、燈具或設備都要登錄投影面積與重量，由結構工程師確認累計值仍在設計範圍內，才可安裝。","observationEn":"Site practice: Set up a register of attachments: every new antenna, light or device records its projected area and weight, and installation proceeds only after the structural engineer confirms the cumulative total is within design.","failure":"注意干擾：若後續加裝天線、照明或廣告物而未重新計算受風面積，實積率上升會讓風力超出設計；圓形段若出現渦流共振，細長的上部會產生持續擺動，對天線與連接件造成疲勞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adding antennas, lighting or signage later without recalculating wind area raises the solidity and pushes wind force beyond design; vortex resonance in the circular segment would make the slender top sway persistently, fatiguing antennas and connections. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以風洞試驗量測不同高度斷面的阻力係數與實積率影響，並確認圓形段沒有明顯的渦流共振；分析模型要逐段輸入桿件投影面積，與風洞結果比較基底剪力與彎矩，並檢查天線、維修平台等附掛物增加的受風面積。","textEn":"Measure drag coefficients and solidity effects for sections at different heights in the wind tunnel and confirm that the circular segment shows no marked vortex resonance; enter member projected areas segment by segment in the analysis model, compare base shear and moment with the wind-tunnel results, and account for added area from antennas and maintenance platforms.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立附掛物登錄制度：任何新增天線、燈具或設備都要登錄投影面積與重量，由結構工程師確認累計值仍在設計範圍內，才可安裝。","textEn":"Set up a register of attachments: every new antenna, light or device records its projected area and weight, and installation proceeds only after the structural engineer confirms the cumulative total is within design.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「三角形基底、圓形頂部與格構風力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Triangular base, circular top and wind on a lattice\"?","options":["以風洞試驗量測不同高度斷面的阻力係數與實積率影響，並確認圓形段沒有明顯的渦流共振。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","地震後只要外觀沒有明顯損壞，施工中的結構就可以立即復工。"],"optionsEn":["Measure drag coefficients and solidity effects for sections at different heights in the wind tunnel and confirm that the circular segment shows no marked vortex resonance.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If there is no visible damage after an earthquake, work on an unfinished structure can resume immediately."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以風洞試驗量測不同高度斷面的阻力係數與實積率影響，並確認圓形段沒有明顯的渦流共振；分析模型要逐段輸入桿件投影面積，與風洞結果比較基底剪力與彎矩，並檢查天線、維修平台等附掛物增加的受風面積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure drag coefficients and solidity effects for sections at different heights in the wind tunnel and confirm that the circular segment shows no marked vortex resonance; enter member projected areas segment by segment in the analysis model, compare base shear and moment with the wind-tunnel results, and account for added area from antennas and maintenance platforms. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b024-v13-04","title":"三角形基底、圓形頂部與格構風力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Triangular base, circular top and wind on a lattice: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「三角形到圓形的斷面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Triangle-to-circle section” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若後續加裝天線、照明或廣告物而未重新計算受風面積，實積率上升會讓風力超出設計；圓形段若出現渦流共振，細長的上部會產生持續擺動，對天線與連接件造成疲勞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adding antennas, lighting or signage later without recalculating wind area raises the solidity and pushes wind force beyond design; vortex resonance in the circular segment would make the slender top sway persistently, fatiguing antennas and connections. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：塔身是鋼管桁架而非實心外牆，風力取決於桿件的投影面積與實積率，而不是整個輪廓面積。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The body is a tubular steel truss rather than a solid skin, so wind force depends on member projected area and solidity ratio rather than on the whole outline.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「格構塔透風，所以風力可以忽略。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A lattice tower lets the wind through, so wind force can be ignored.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若後續加裝天線、照明或廣告物而未重新計算受風面積，實積率上升會讓風力超出設計；圓形段若出現渦流共振，細長的上部會產生持續擺動，對天線與連接件造成疲勞。","textEn":"Adding antennas, lighting or signage later without recalculating wind area raises the solidity and pushes wind force beyond design; vortex resonance in the circular segment would make the slender top sway persistently, fatiguing antennas and connections.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「三角形基底、圓形頂部與格構風力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Triangular base, circular top and wind on a lattice\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若後續加裝天線、照明或廣告物而未重新計算受風面積，實積率上升會讓風力超出設計；圓形段若出現渦流共振，細長的上部會產生持續擺動，對天線與連接件造成疲勞。","心柱是用來支撐鋼塔重量的主柱。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Adding antennas, lighting or signage later without recalculating wind area raises the solidity and pushes wind force beyond design.","The central column is the main column that carries the steel tower's weight."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若後續加裝天線、照明或廣告物而未重新計算受風面積，實積率上升會讓風力超出設計；圓形段若出現渦流共振，細長的上部會產生持續擺動，對天線與連接件造成疲勞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adding antennas, lighting or signage later without recalculating wind area raises the solidity and pushes wind force beyond design; vortex resonance in the circular segment would make the slender top sway persistently, fatiguing antennas and connections. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b024-v13-05","title":"心柱與鋼塔的相位差減振：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Out-of-phase damping between central column and tower: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「心柱制振」如何影響東京晴空塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shimbashira vibration control” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tokyo Skytree”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"塔的中央是一根直徑約 8 m 的鋼筋混凝土圓筒心柱，內設逃生樓梯，高度約到 375 m，與外側鋼塔在結構上分離。心柱在約 125 m 以下與鋼塔固結，125 m 至 375 m 之間則以油壓阻尼器連接；地震或強風時心柱與鋼塔的週期不同，擺動出現相位差，阻尼器在兩者的相對運動中消耗能量。設計概念取自五重塔的中心柱，公開資料稱可減少地震反應約 40% 至 50%。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「心柱制振」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"At the centre stands a reinforced concrete cylinder about 8 m in diameter, housing an escape stair and rising to about 375 m, structurally separate from the outer steel tower. The column is fixed to the tower below about 125 m and connected by oil dampers between 125 m and 375 m; in an earthquake or strong wind the column and tower have different periods and sway out of phase, so the dampers dissipate energy in their relative motion. The concept is drawn from the central pillar of five-storey pagodas, and public sources state seismic response reductions of about 40% to 50%. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Shimbashira vibration control” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：阻尼器力 F = c·Δv，Δv = 2π·f·Δx。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Damper force F = c·Δv with Δv = 2π·f·Δx.","failure":"常見誤解：「心柱是用來支撐鋼塔重量的主柱。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The central column is the main column that carries the steel tower's weight.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「心柱制振」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Shimbashira vibration control”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-05-k1","title":"心柱與鋼塔的相位差減振","titleEn":"Out-of-phase damping between central column and tower","text":"塔的中央是一根直徑約 8 m 的鋼筋混凝土圓筒心柱，內設逃生樓梯，高度約到 375 m，與外側鋼塔在結構上分離。心柱在約 125 m 以下與鋼塔固結，125 m 至 375 m 之間則以油壓阻尼器連接；地震或強風時心柱與鋼塔的週期不同，擺動出現相位差，阻尼器在兩者的相對運動中消耗能量。","textEn":"At the centre stands a reinforced concrete cylinder about 8 m in diameter, housing an escape stair and rising to about 375 m, structurally separate from the outer steel tower. The column is fixed to the tower below about 125 m and connected by oil dampers between 125 m and 375 m; in an earthquake or strong wind the column and tower have different periods and sway out of phase, so the dampers dissipate energy in their relative motion.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：心柱是用來支撐鋼塔重量的主柱。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The central column is the main column that carries the steel tower's weight. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「心柱與鋼塔的相位差減振」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Out-of-phase damping between central column and tower\" is correct?","options":["心柱是用來支撐鋼塔重量的主柱。","鋼管越粗越厚就越安全，接頭細節不重要。","塔的中央是一根直徑約 8 m 的鋼筋混凝土圓筒心柱，內設逃生樓梯，高度約到 375 m，與外側鋼塔在結構上分離。"],"optionsEn":["The central column is the main column that carries the steel tower's weight.","The bigger and thicker the tube, the safer it is; joint details do not matter.","At the centre stands a reinforced concrete cylinder about 8 m in diameter, housing an escape stair and rising to about 375 m, structurally separate from the outer steel tower."],"answer":2,"explanation":"塔的中央是一根直徑約 8 m 的鋼筋混凝土圓筒心柱，內設逃生樓梯，高度約到 375 m，與外側鋼塔在結構上分離。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"At the centre stands a reinforced concrete cylinder about 8 m in diameter, housing an escape stair and rising to about 375 m, structurally separate from the outer steel tower. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b024-v13-06","title":"心柱與鋼塔的相位差減振：定量估算","titleEn":"Out-of-phase damping between central column and tower: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「心柱制振」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shimbashira vibration control” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：阻尼器力 F = c·Δv，Δv = 2π·f·Δx。若兩者相對位移振幅 Δx = 0.10 m、頻率 f = 0.3 Hz，Δv ≈ 0.188 m/s；阻尼係數 c = 5,000 kN·s/m 時 F ≈ 942 kN，每循環消耗能量 E = π·c·ω·Δx² ≈ π×5,000×1.885×0.01 ≈ 296 kJ。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Damper force F = c·Δv with Δv = 2π·f·Δx. For a relative amplitude Δx = 0.10 m at f = 0.3 Hz, Δv ≈ 0.188 m/s; with c = 5,000 kN·s/m, F ≈ 942 kN, and the energy dissipated per cycle is E = π·c·ω·Δx² ≈ π×5,000×1.885×0.01 ≈ 296 kJ. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以時間歷程分析比較有無阻尼器連接時的頂部加速度、基底剪力與兩者相對位移，確認相對位移落在阻尼器行程內；也要檢查心柱與鋼塔的週期比，若兩者太接近就不會產生足夠的相位差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare top acceleration, base shear and relative displacement with and without the damper connection in time-history analyses, confirming relative displacement stays within damper stroke; also check the period ratio of column and tower, since periods too close together will not produce enough phase difference.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"阻尼器力 F = c·Δv，Δv = 2π·f·Δx。若兩者相對位移振幅 Δx = 0.10 m、頻率 f = 0.3 Hz，Δv ≈ 0.188 m/s；阻尼係數 c = 5,000 kN·s/m 時 F ≈ 942 kN，每循環消耗能量 E = π·c·ω·Δx² ≈ π×5,000×1.885×0.01 ≈ 296 kJ。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Damper force F = c·Δv with Δv = 2π·f·Δx. For a relative amplitude Δx = 0.10 m at f = 0.3 Hz, Δv ≈ 0.188 m/s; with c = 5,000 kN·s/m, F ≈ 942 kN, and the energy dissipated per cycle is E = π·c·ω·Δx² ≈ π×5,000×1.885×0.01 ≈ 296 kJ. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「心柱與鋼塔的相位差減振」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Out-of-phase damping between central column and tower\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器力 F = c·Δv，Δv = 2π·f·Δx。","鋼構安裝只要每段都對準設計座標，量測時間不重要。","阻尼器的力量越大越好，不需要限制。"],"optionsEn":["Damper force F = c·Δv with Δv = 2π·f·Δx.","As long as each segment is set to design coordinates, the time of surveying does not matter.","The larger a damper's force the better, so it needs no limit."],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻尼器力 F = c·Δv，Δv = 2π·f·Δx。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Damper force F = c·Δv with Δv = 2π·f·Δx. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b024-v13-07","title":"心柱與鋼塔的相位差減振：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Out-of-phase damping between central column and tower: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「心柱制振」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shimbashira vibration control” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以時間歷程分析比較有無阻尼器連接時的頂部加速度、基底剪力與兩者相對位移，確認相對位移落在阻尼器行程內；也要檢查心柱與鋼塔的週期比，若兩者太接近就不會產生足夠的相位差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare top acceleration, base shear and relative displacement with and without the damper connection in time-history analyses, confirming relative displacement stays within damper stroke; also check the period ratio of column and tower, since periods too close together will not produce enough phase difference. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：心柱與鋼塔的相對位移、阻尼器行程與淨空要在同一張圖上管理，任何在兩者之間新增的管線或平台都必須保留滑動或可撓接頭；阻尼器的型號、數量與試驗資料列入交接文件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Manage relative displacement, damper stroke and clearance between column and tower on one drawing, require any new services or platforms bridging the gap to keep sliding or flexible joints, and include damper models, numbers and test data in the handover documents.","failure":"注意干擾：若心柱與鋼塔之間的淨空不足，大地震時兩者可能碰撞；阻尼器若漏油或卡死，心柱會變成單純的附加質量或剛性連接，減振效果消失，甚至在某些頻率放大反應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Insufficient clearance between column and tower can let them collide in a major earthquake; if dampers leak or seize, the column becomes mere added mass or a rigid link, the damping benefit disappears and response may even amplify at some frequencies. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以時間歷程分析比較有無阻尼器連接時的頂部加速度、基底剪力與兩者相對位移，確認相對位移落在阻尼器行程內；也要檢查心柱與鋼塔的週期比，若兩者太接近就不會產生足夠的相位差。","textEn":"Compare top acceleration, base shear and relative displacement with and without the damper connection in time-history analyses, confirming relative displacement stays within damper stroke; also check the period ratio of column and tower, since periods too close together will not produce enough phase difference.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"心柱與鋼塔的相對位移、阻尼器行程與淨空要在同一張圖上管理，任何在兩者之間新增的管線或平台都必須保留滑動或可撓接頭；阻尼器的型號、數量與試驗資料列入交接文件。","textEn":"Manage relative displacement, damper stroke and clearance between column and tower on one drawing, require any new services or platforms bridging the gap to keep sliding or flexible joints, and include damper models, numbers and test data in the handover documents.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「心柱與鋼塔的相位差減振」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Out-of-phase damping between central column and tower\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以時間歷程分析比較有無阻尼器連接時的頂部加速度、基底剪力與兩者相對位移，確認相對位移落在阻尼器行程內。","落冰只是維護清潔問題，和結構工程無關。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Compare top acceleration, base shear and relative displacement with and without the damper connection in time-history analyses, confirming relative displacement stays within damper stroke.","Falling ice is only a cleaning issue and has nothing to do with structural engineering."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以時間歷程分析比較有無阻尼器連接時的頂部加速度、基底剪力與兩者相對位移，確認相對位移落在阻尼器行程內；也要檢查心柱與鋼塔的週期比，若兩者太接近就不會產生足夠的相位差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare top acceleration, base shear and relative displacement with and without the damper connection in time-history analyses, confirming relative displacement stays within damper stroke; also check the period ratio of column and tower, since periods too close together will not produce enough phase difference. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b024-v13-08","title":"心柱與鋼塔的相位差減振：失效診斷","titleEn":"Out-of-phase damping between central column and tower: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「心柱制振」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shimbashira vibration control” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若心柱與鋼塔之間的淨空不足，大地震時兩者可能碰撞；阻尼器若漏油或卡死，心柱會變成單純的附加質量或剛性連接，減振效果消失，甚至在某些頻率放大反應。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Insufficient clearance between column and tower can let them collide in a major earthquake; if dampers leak or seize, the column becomes mere added mass or a rigid link, the damping benefit disappears and response may even amplify at some frequencies. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計概念取自五重塔的中心柱，公開資料稱可減少地震反應約 40% 至 50%。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The concept is drawn from the central pillar of five-storey pagodas, and public sources state seismic response reductions of about 40% to 50%.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「心柱是用來支撐鋼塔重量的主柱。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The central column is the main column that carries the steel tower's weight.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若心柱與鋼塔之間的淨空不足，大地震時兩者可能碰撞；阻尼器若漏油或卡死，心柱會變成單純的附加質量或剛性連接，減振效果消失，甚至在某些頻率放大反應。","textEn":"Insufficient clearance between column and tower can let them collide in a major earthquake; if dampers leak or seize, the column becomes mere added mass or a rigid link, the damping benefit disappears and response may even amplify at some frequencies.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「心柱與鋼塔的相位差減振」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Out-of-phase damping between central column and tower\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鋼管越粗越厚就越安全，接頭細節不重要。","若心柱與鋼塔之間的淨空不足，大地震時兩者可能碰撞；阻尼器若漏油或卡死，心柱會變成單純的附加質量或剛性連接，減振效果消失，甚至在某些頻率放大反應。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The bigger and thicker the tube, the safer it is; joint details do not matter.","Insufficient clearance between column and tower can let them collide in a major earthquake."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若心柱與鋼塔之間的淨空不足，大地震時兩者可能碰撞；阻尼器若漏油或卡死，心柱會變成單純的附加質量或剛性連接，減振效果消失，甚至在某些頻率放大反應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Insufficient clearance between column and tower can let them collide in a major earthquake; if dampers leak or seize, the column becomes mere added mass or a rigid link, the damping benefit disappears and response may even amplify at some frequencies. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b024-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「高強度鋼管構材與分歧接頭」與「節狀連續壁樁的摩擦與拉拔」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"High-strength tubular members and branch joints\" and \"Friction and uplift in knuckle wall piles\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b024-v13-09","title":"高強度鋼管構材與分歧接頭：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"High-strength tubular members and branch joints: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「直徑 2.3 m 鋼管」如何影響東京晴空塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “2.3 m diameter steel tubes” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tokyo Skytree”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"晴空塔的主要構材用鋼管而非 H 型鋼，主要接頭以焊接的分歧接頭（管對管直接相貫）組成，以減輕重量並提高耐震性；最粗的鋼管直徑約 2.3 m、厚約 10 cm，公開資料指出單根約 29 公噸，並使用約為一般鋼材兩倍強度的高強度鋼。圓管在各方向的抗彎與抗挫屈性能相同，受風面積也較小；但相貫接頭的應力集中明顯，焊接幾何與熱影響區的韌性是設計重點。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「直徑 2.3 m 鋼管」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Skytree's main members are steel tubes rather than H-sections, joined mostly by welded branch joints where tube meets tube directly, to save weight and improve seismic performance; the largest tubes are about 2.3 m in diameter and about 10 cm thick, one such piece weighing about 29 t according to public sources, in high-strength steel of roughly twice ordinary strength. A circular tube has equal bending and buckling resistance in every direction and less wind area, but stress concentrations at intersecting joints are pronounced, so weld geometry and heat-affected-zone toughness are key design concerns. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “2.3 m diameter steel tubes” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：鋼管面積 A = π·(D − t)·t = π×2.2×0.1 ≈ 0.691 m²，每公尺重 0.691×7,850 ≈ 5,430 kg，29 t 的構材長約 5.3 m；以降伏強度 630 MPa 計，全斷面降伏軸力約 0.691×630 ≈ 435 MN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Tube area A = π·(D − t)·t = π×2.2×0.1 ≈ 0.691 m², about 5,430 kg per metre, so a 29 t piece is about 5.3 m long; at a yield strength of 630 MPa the squash load is about 0.691×630 ≈ 435 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼管越粗越厚就越安全，接頭細節不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The bigger and thicker the tube, the safer it is; joint details do not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「直徑 2.3 m 鋼管」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “2.3 m diameter steel tubes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-09-k1","title":"高強度鋼管構材與分歧接頭","titleEn":"High-strength tubular members and branch joints","text":"晴空塔的主要構材用鋼管而非 H 型鋼，主要接頭以焊接的分歧接頭（管對管直接相貫）組成，以減輕重量並提高耐震性；最粗的鋼管直徑約 2.3 m、厚約 10 cm，公開資料指出單根約 29 公噸，並使用約為一般鋼材兩倍強度的高強度鋼。圓管在各方向的抗彎與抗挫屈性能相同，受風面積也較小；但相貫接頭的應力集中明顯，焊接幾何與熱影響區的韌性是設計重點。","textEn":"Skytree's main members are steel tubes rather than H-sections, joined mostly by welded branch joints where tube meets tube directly, to save weight and improve seismic performance; the largest tubes are about 2.3 m in diameter and about 10 cm thick, one such piece weighing about 29 t according to public sources, in high-strength steel of roughly twice ordinary strength. A circular tube has equal bending and buckling resistance in every direction and less wind area, but stress concentrations at intersecting joints are pronounced, so weld geometry and heat-affected-zone toughness are key design concerns.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼管越粗越厚就越安全，接頭細節不重要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The bigger and thicker the tube, the safer it is; joint details do not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高強度鋼管構材與分歧接頭」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"High-strength tubular members and branch joints\" is correct?","options":["晴空塔的主要構材用鋼管而非 H 型鋼，主要接頭以焊接的分歧接頭（管對管直接相貫）組成，以減輕重量並提高耐震性。","鋼管越粗越厚就越安全，接頭細節不重要。","塔很重，所以基礎只需要考慮下壓，不會受拉。"],"optionsEn":["Skytree's main members are steel tubes rather than H-sections, joined mostly by welded branch joints where tube meets tube directly, to save weight and improve seismic performance.","The bigger and thicker the tube, the safer it is; joint details do not matter.","The tower is heavy, so its foundation only needs to resist compression and never tension."],"answer":0,"explanation":"晴空塔的主要構材用鋼管而非 H 型鋼，主要接頭以焊接的分歧接頭（管對管直接相貫）組成，以減輕重量並提高耐震性；最粗的鋼管直徑約 2.3 m、厚約 10 cm，公開資料指出單根約 29 公噸，並使用約為一般鋼材兩倍強度的高強度鋼。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Skytree's main members are steel tubes rather than H-sections, joined mostly by welded branch joints where tube meets tube directly, to save weight and improve seismic performance; the largest tubes are about 2.3 m in diameter and about 10 cm thick, one such piece weighing about 29 t according to public sources, in high-strength steel of roughly twice ordinary strength. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b024-v13-10","title":"高強度鋼管構材與分歧接頭：定量估算","titleEn":"High-strength tubular members and branch joints: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「直徑 2.3 m 鋼管」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “2.3 m diameter steel tubes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：鋼管面積 A = π·(D − t)·t = π×2.2×0.1 ≈ 0.691 m²，每公尺重 0.691×7,850 ≈ 5,430 kg，29 t 的構材長約 5.3 m；以降伏強度 630 MPa 計，全斷面降伏軸力約 0.691×630 ≈ 435 MN。徑厚比 D/t = 23，屬局部挫屈不易發生的厚實斷面。強度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Tube area A = π·(D − t)·t = π×2.2×0.1 ≈ 0.691 m², about 5,430 kg per metre, so a 29 t piece is about 5.3 m long; at a yield strength of 630 MPa the squash load is about 0.691×630 ≈ 435 MN. With D/t = 23 the section is stocky and unlikely to buckle locally. The strength is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分歧接頭以有限元素分析求熱點應力，並以縮尺或足尺試體驗證應力集中係數與疲勞強度；工廠焊接全數做超音波檢測，厚板焊接記錄預熱與層間溫度，鋼材以夏比衝擊試驗確認低溫韌性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Obtain hot-spot stresses at branch joints by finite-element analysis and verify stress concentration factors and fatigue strength on scaled or full-size specimens; ultrasonically test all shop welds, record preheat and interpass temperatures for thick welds, and confirm low-temperature toughness of the steel by Charpy impact tests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"鋼管面積 A = π·(D − t)·t = π×2.2×0.1 ≈ 0.691 m²，每公尺重 0.691×7,850 ≈ 5,430 kg，29 t 的構材長約 5.3 m；以降伏強度 630 MPa 計，全斷面降伏軸力約 0.691×630 ≈ 435 MN。徑厚比 D/t = 23，屬局部挫屈不易發生的厚實斷面。強度為教學假設。","textEn":"Tube area A = π·(D − t)·t = π×2.2×0.1 ≈ 0.691 m², about 5,430 kg per metre, so a 29 t piece is about 5.3 m long; at a yield strength of 630 MPa the squash load is about 0.691×630 ≈ 435 MN. With D/t = 23 the section is stocky and unlikely to buckle locally. The strength is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高強度鋼管構材與分歧接頭」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"High-strength tubular members and branch joints\", which statement holds?","options":["在豎井內頂升比較安全，所以不需要另做結構分析。","鋼管面積 A = π·(D − t)·t = π×2.2×0.1 ≈ 0.691 m²，每公尺重 0.691×7,850 ≈ 5,430 kg，29 t 的構材長約 5.3 m。","地震後只要外觀沒有明顯損壞，施工中的結構就可以立即復工。"],"optionsEn":["Lifting inside the shaft is safer, so no separate structural analysis is needed.","Tube area A = π·(D − t)·t = π×2.2×0.1 ≈ 0.691 m², about 5,430 kg per metre, so a 29 t piece is about 5.3 m long.","If there is no visible damage after an earthquake, work on an unfinished structure can resume immediately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鋼管面積 A = π·(D − t)·t = π×2.2×0.1 ≈ 0.691 m²，每公尺重 0.691×7,850 ≈ 5,430 kg，29 t 的構材長約 5.3 m；以降伏強度 630 MPa 計，全斷面降伏軸力約 0.691×630 ≈ 435 MN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Tube area A = π·(D − t)·t = π×2.2×0.1 ≈ 0.691 m², about 5,430 kg per metre, so a 29 t piece is about 5.3 m long; at a yield strength of 630 MPa the squash load is about 0.691×630 ≈ 435 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b024-v13-11","title":"高強度鋼管構材與分歧接頭：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"High-strength tubular members and branch joints: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「直徑 2.3 m 鋼管」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “2.3 m diameter steel tubes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分歧接頭以有限元素分析求熱點應力，並以縮尺或足尺試體驗證應力集中係數與疲勞強度；工廠焊接全數做超音波檢測，厚板焊接記錄預熱與層間溫度，鋼材以夏比衝擊試驗確認低溫韌性。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Obtain hot-spot stresses at branch joints by finite-element analysis and verify stress concentration factors and fatigue strength on scaled or full-size specimens; ultrasonically test all shop welds, record preheat and interpass temperatures for thick welds, and confirm low-temperature toughness of the steel by Charpy impact tests. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：每一個分歧接頭要有焊接程序書、熱點應力計算與檢測紀錄，焊趾修整列為檢驗項目；高強度鋼的焊材、熱輸入範圍與預熱溫度由材料與焊接工程師共同簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Give every branch joint a welding procedure, hot-spot stress calculation and inspection record, with weld-toe dressing as an inspection item; consumables, heat-input range and preheat for the high-strength steel are signed off jointly by the materials and welding engineers.","failure":"注意干擾：相貫接頭若焊趾成形不良或有未熔合，風致反覆應力會在熱點處引發疲勞裂縫；高強度鋼若焊接熱輸入控制不當，熱影響區變脆，地震時可能在接頭附近脆性斷裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Poor weld-toe profiles or lack of fusion at intersecting joints let repeated wind stresses start fatigue cracks at hot spots; poorly controlled heat input on high-strength steel embrittles the heat-affected zone, risking brittle fracture near joints in an earthquake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分歧接頭以有限元素分析求熱點應力，並以縮尺或足尺試體驗證應力集中係數與疲勞強度；工廠焊接全數做超音波檢測，厚板焊接記錄預熱與層間溫度，鋼材以夏比衝擊試驗確認低溫韌性。","textEn":"Obtain hot-spot stresses at branch joints by finite-element analysis and verify stress concentration factors and fatigue strength on scaled or full-size specimens; ultrasonically test all shop welds, record preheat and interpass temperatures for thick welds, and confirm low-temperature toughness of the steel by Charpy impact tests.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"每一個分歧接頭要有焊接程序書、熱點應力計算與檢測紀錄，焊趾修整列為檢驗項目；高強度鋼的焊材、熱輸入範圍與預熱溫度由材料與焊接工程師共同簽認。","textEn":"Give every branch joint a welding procedure, hot-spot stress calculation and inspection record, with weld-toe dressing as an inspection item; consumables, heat-input range and preheat for the high-strength steel are signed off jointly by the materials and welding engineers.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高強度鋼管構材與分歧接頭」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"High-strength tubular members and branch joints\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","主鋼管很厚，所以腐蝕對鋼管塔沒有影響。","分歧接頭以有限元素分析求熱點應力，並以縮尺或足尺試體驗證應力集中係數與疲勞強度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The main tubes are very thick, so corrosion does not matter for a tube tower.","Obtain hot-spot stresses at branch joints by finite-element analysis and verify stress concentration factors and fatigue strength on scaled or full-size specimens."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分歧接頭以有限元素分析求熱點應力，並以縮尺或足尺試體驗證應力集中係數與疲勞強度；工廠焊接全數做超音波檢測，厚板焊接記錄預熱與層間溫度，鋼材以夏比衝擊試驗確認低溫韌性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Obtain hot-spot stresses at branch joints by finite-element analysis and verify stress concentration factors and fatigue strength on scaled or full-size specimens; ultrasonically test all shop welds, record preheat and interpass temperatures for thick welds, and confirm low-temperature toughness of the steel by Charpy impact tests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b024-v13-12","title":"高強度鋼管構材與分歧接頭：失效診斷","titleEn":"High-strength tubular members and branch joints: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「直徑 2.3 m 鋼管」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “2.3 m diameter steel tubes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"相貫接頭若焊趾成形不良或有未熔合，風致反覆應力會在熱點處引發疲勞裂縫；高強度鋼若焊接熱輸入控制不當，熱影響區變脆，地震時可能在接頭附近脆性斷裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Poor weld-toe profiles or lack of fusion at intersecting joints let repeated wind stresses start fatigue cracks at hot spots; poorly controlled heat input on high-strength steel embrittles the heat-affected zone, risking brittle fracture near joints in an earthquake. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓管在各方向的抗彎與抗挫屈性能相同，受風面積也較小；但相貫接頭的應力集中明顯，焊接幾何與熱影響區的韌性是設計重點。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A circular tube has equal bending and buckling resistance in every direction and less wind area, but stress concentrations at intersecting joints are pronounced, so weld geometry and heat-affected-zone toughness are key design concerns.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼管越粗越厚就越安全，接頭細節不重要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The bigger and thicker the tube, the safer it is; joint details do not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"相貫接頭若焊趾成形不良或有未熔合，風致反覆應力會在熱點處引發疲勞裂縫；高強度鋼若焊接熱輸入控制不當，熱影響區變脆，地震時可能在接頭附近脆性斷裂。","textEn":"Poor weld-toe profiles or lack of fusion at intersecting joints let repeated wind stresses start fatigue cracks at hot spots; poorly controlled heat input on high-strength steel embrittles the heat-affected zone, risking brittle fracture near joints in an earthquake.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高強度鋼管構材與分歧接頭」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"High-strength tubular members and branch joints\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["相貫接頭若焊趾成形不良或有未熔合，風致反覆應力會在熱點處引發疲勞裂縫；高強度鋼若焊接熱輸入控制不當，熱影響區變脆，地震時可能在接頭附近脆性斷裂。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","塔很重，所以基礎只需要考慮下壓，不會受拉。"],"optionsEn":["Poor weld-toe profiles or lack of fusion at intersecting joints let repeated wind stresses start fatigue cracks at hot spots.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The tower is heavy, so its foundation only needs to resist compression and never tension."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相貫接頭若焊趾成形不良或有未熔合，風致反覆應力會在熱點處引發疲勞裂縫；高強度鋼若焊接熱輸入控制不當，熱影響區變脆，地震時可能在接頭附近脆性斷裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Poor weld-toe profiles or lack of fusion at intersecting joints let repeated wind stresses start fatigue cracks at hot spots; poorly controlled heat input on high-strength steel embrittles the heat-affected zone, risking brittle fracture near joints in an earthquake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b024-v13-13","title":"節狀連續壁樁的摩擦與拉拔：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Friction and uplift in knuckle wall piles: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「節狀壁樁」如何影響東京晴空塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Knuckle wall piles” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tokyo Skytree”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"晴空塔建在隅田川附近的沖積地層上，三支腳柱下方採用節狀壁樁（knuckle wall），以場鑄混凝土壁樁深入地下約 50 m，壁面每隔一段設突出的「節」，並以放射狀相互連結。節像錨一樣嵌入土層，同時增加下壓時的承壓面與上拔時的抵抗面；三角形配置使強風或地震時迎風腳可能減壓甚至受拉，所以基礎的拉拔能力與下壓能力同樣重要。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「節狀壁樁」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Skytree stands on alluvial ground near the Sumida River, and beneath its three legs are knuckle wall piles: cast-in-place concrete wall piles reaching about 50 m deep, with projecting knuckles at intervals along the wall and radial interconnection. The knuckles key into the soil like anchors, adding bearing area in compression and resisting area in uplift; because the triangular layout can unload or even lift the windward leg in strong wind or earthquakes, the foundation's uplift capacity matters as much as its compressive capacity. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Knuckle wall piles” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：壁樁容量 Q = 周長×L×f_s + Σ節承壓。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Wall-pile capacity Q = perimeter×L×f_s + Σ knuckle bearing.","failure":"常見誤解：「塔很重，所以基礎只需要考慮下壓，不會受拉。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The tower is heavy, so its foundation only needs to resist compression and never tension.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「節狀壁樁」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Knuckle wall piles”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-13-k1","title":"節狀連續壁樁的摩擦與拉拔","titleEn":"Friction and uplift in knuckle wall piles","text":"晴空塔建在隅田川附近的沖積地層上，三支腳柱下方採用節狀壁樁（knuckle wall），以場鑄混凝土壁樁深入地下約 50 m，壁面每隔一段設突出的「節」，並以放射狀相互連結。節像錨一樣嵌入土層，同時增加下壓時的承壓面與上拔時的抵抗面；三角形配置使強風或地震時迎風腳可能減壓甚至受拉，所以基礎的拉拔能力與下壓能力同樣重要。","textEn":"Skytree stands on alluvial ground near the Sumida River, and beneath its three legs are knuckle wall piles: cast-in-place concrete wall piles reaching about 50 m deep, with projecting knuckles at intervals along the wall and radial interconnection. The knuckles key into the soil like anchors, adding bearing area in compression and resisting area in uplift; because the triangular layout can unload or even lift the windward leg in strong wind or earthquakes, the foundation's uplift capacity matters as much as its compressive capacity.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：塔很重，所以基礎只需要考慮下壓，不會受拉。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The tower is heavy, so its foundation only needs to resist compression and never tension. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「節狀連續壁樁的摩擦與拉拔」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Friction and uplift in knuckle wall piles\" is correct?","options":["塔很重，所以基礎只需要考慮下壓，不會受拉。","晴空塔建在隅田川附近的沖積地層上，三支腳柱下方採用節狀壁樁（knuckle wall），以場鑄混凝土壁樁深入地下約 50 m，壁面每隔一段設突出的「節」，並以放射狀相互連結。","鋼構安裝只要每段都對準設計座標，量測時間不重要。"],"optionsEn":["The tower is heavy, so its foundation only needs to resist compression and never tension.","Skytree stands on alluvial ground near the Sumida River, and beneath its three legs are knuckle wall piles: cast-in-place concrete wall piles reaching about 50 m deep, with projecting knuckles at intervals along the wall and radial interconnection.","As long as each segment is set to design coordinates, the time of surveying does not matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"晴空塔建在隅田川附近的沖積地層上，三支腳柱下方採用節狀壁樁（knuckle wall），以場鑄混凝土壁樁深入地下約 50 m，壁面每隔一段設突出的「節」，並以放射狀相互連結。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Skytree stands on alluvial ground near the Sumida River, and beneath its three legs are knuckle wall piles: cast-in-place concrete wall piles reaching about 50 m deep, with projecting knuckles at intervals along the wall and radial interconnection. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b024-v13-14","title":"節狀連續壁樁的摩擦與拉拔：定量估算","titleEn":"Friction and uplift in knuckle wall piles: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「節狀壁樁」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Knuckle wall piles” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：壁樁容量 Q = 周長×L×f_s + Σ節承壓。壁段 1.2 m × 6 m（周長 14.4 m）、L = 50 m、f_s = 80 kPa：側摩擦 14.4×50×0.08 = 57.6 MN；3 個節各外凸 0.4 m，承壓面積 0.4×14.4 = 5.76 m²、承壓 1.5 MPa，各約 8.6 MN，合計約 25.9 MN；總容量約 83.5 MN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Wall-pile capacity Q = perimeter×L×f_s + Σ knuckle bearing. For a 1.2 m × 6 m panel (14.4 m perimeter), L = 50 m and f_s = 80 kPa, side friction is 14.4×50×0.08 = 57.6 MN; three knuckles each projecting 0.4 m give 0.4×14.4 = 5.76 m² of bearing at 1.5 MPa, about 8.6 MN each or 25.9 MN together, for a total of about 83.5 MN. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以試驗樁做下壓與拉拔載重試驗，量測節的貢獻與側摩擦分布；施工時以超音波量測壁槽形狀，確認節的位置與尺寸符合設計，並記錄穩定液性質與混凝土澆置量，比對理論體積以發現坍孔或縮頸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Load-test trial piles in compression and uplift to measure the knuckle contribution and side-friction distribution; during construction profile the trench ultrasonically to confirm knuckle position and size, and log slurry properties and concrete volume against theoretical volume to detect collapse or necking.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"壁樁容量 Q = 周長×L×f_s + Σ節承壓。壁段 1.2 m × 6 m（周長 14.4 m）、L = 50 m、f_s = 80 kPa：側摩擦 14.4×50×0.08 = 57.6 MN；3 個節各外凸 0.4 m，承壓面積 0.4×14.4 = 5.76 m²、承壓 1.5 MPa，各約 8.6 MN，合計約 25.9 MN；總容量約 83.5 MN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Wall-pile capacity Q = perimeter×L×f_s + Σ knuckle bearing. For a 1.2 m × 6 m panel (14.4 m perimeter), L = 50 m and f_s = 80 kPa, side friction is 14.4×50×0.08 = 57.6 MN; three knuckles each projecting 0.4 m give 0.4×14.4 = 5.76 m² of bearing at 1.5 MPa, about 8.6 MN each or 25.9 MN together, for a total of about 83.5 MN. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「節狀連續壁樁的摩擦與拉拔」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Friction and uplift in knuckle wall piles\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器的力量越大越好，不需要限制。","落冰只是維護清潔問題，和結構工程無關。","壁樁容量 Q = 周長×L×f_s + Σ節承壓。"],"optionsEn":["The larger a damper's force the better, so it needs no limit.","Falling ice is only a cleaning issue and has nothing to do with structural engineering.","Wall-pile capacity Q = perimeter×L×f_s + Σ knuckle bearing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"壁樁容量 Q = 周長×L×f_s + Σ節承壓。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Wall-pile capacity Q = perimeter×L×f_s + Σ knuckle bearing. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b024-v13-15","title":"節狀連續壁樁的摩擦與拉拔：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Friction and uplift in knuckle wall piles: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「節狀壁樁」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Knuckle wall piles” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以試驗樁做下壓與拉拔載重試驗，量測節的貢獻與側摩擦分布；施工時以超音波量測壁槽形狀，確認節的位置與尺寸符合設計，並記錄穩定液性質與混凝土澆置量，比對理論體積以發現坍孔或縮頸。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Load-test trial piles in compression and uplift to measure the knuckle contribution and side-friction distribution; during construction profile the trench ultrasonically to confirm knuckle position and size, and log slurry properties and concrete volume against theoretical volume to detect collapse or necking. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：每片壁樁的開挖斷面量測、節位置照片與澆置紀錄要逐片歸檔；拉拔試驗結果未達標前，不得進行腳柱基礎的上部施工，此為結構設計者簽認的停止點。","observationEn":"Site practice: File trench profile measurements, knuckle position photographs and placement records panel by panel; superstructure work on a leg foundation must not start until uplift test results meet the criteria, a hold point signed by the structural designer.","failure":"注意干擾：若節的開挖尺寸不足或被坍落土填塞，節的承壓貢獻大減，拉拔容量可能遠低於設計；放射狀連結若在施工縫處接合不良，三支腳柱的基礎無法共同作用，差異沉陷與傾斜風險增加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If knuckles are under-excavated or filled with collapsed soil, their bearing contribution drops sharply and uplift capacity can fall far below design; poor joints in the radial interconnection keep the three leg foundations from acting together, raising the risk of differential settlement and tilt. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以試驗樁做下壓與拉拔載重試驗，量測節的貢獻與側摩擦分布；施工時以超音波量測壁槽形狀，確認節的位置與尺寸符合設計，並記錄穩定液性質與混凝土澆置量，比對理論體積以發現坍孔或縮頸。","textEn":"Load-test trial piles in compression and uplift to measure the knuckle contribution and side-friction distribution; during construction profile the trench ultrasonically to confirm knuckle position and size, and log slurry properties and concrete volume against theoretical volume to detect collapse or necking.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"每片壁樁的開挖斷面量測、節位置照片與澆置紀錄要逐片歸檔；拉拔試驗結果未達標前，不得進行腳柱基礎的上部施工，此為結構設計者簽認的停止點。","textEn":"File trench profile measurements, knuckle position photographs and placement records panel by panel; superstructure work on a leg foundation must not start until uplift test results meet the criteria, a hold point signed by the structural designer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「節狀連續壁樁的摩擦與拉拔」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Friction and uplift in knuckle wall piles\"?","options":["以試驗樁做下壓與拉拔載重試驗，量測節的貢獻與側摩擦分布。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","格構塔透風，所以風力可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Load-test trial piles in compression and uplift to measure the knuckle contribution and side-friction distribution.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A lattice tower lets the wind through, so wind force can be ignored."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以試驗樁做下壓與拉拔載重試驗，量測節的貢獻與側摩擦分布；施工時以超音波量測壁槽形狀，確認節的位置與尺寸符合設計，並記錄穩定液性質與混凝土澆置量，比對理論體積以發現坍孔或縮頸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Load-test trial piles in compression and uplift to measure the knuckle contribution and side-friction distribution; during construction profile the trench ultrasonically to confirm knuckle position and size, and log slurry properties and concrete volume against theoretical volume to detect collapse or necking. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b024-v13-16","title":"節狀連續壁樁的摩擦與拉拔：失效診斷","titleEn":"Friction and uplift in knuckle wall piles: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「節狀壁樁」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Knuckle wall piles” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若節的開挖尺寸不足或被坍落土填塞，節的承壓貢獻大減，拉拔容量可能遠低於設計；放射狀連結若在施工縫處接合不良，三支腳柱的基礎無法共同作用，差異沉陷與傾斜風險增加。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If knuckles are under-excavated or filled with collapsed soil, their bearing contribution drops sharply and uplift capacity can fall far below design; poor joints in the radial interconnection keep the three leg foundations from acting together, raising the risk of differential settlement and tilt. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：節像錨一樣嵌入土層，同時增加下壓時的承壓面與上拔時的抵抗面；三角形配置使強風或地震時迎風腳可能減壓甚至受拉，所以基礎的拉拔能力與下壓能力同樣重要。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The knuckles key into the soil like anchors, adding bearing area in compression and resisting area in uplift; because the triangular layout can unload or even lift the windward leg in strong wind or earthquakes, the foundation's uplift capacity matters as much as its compressive capacity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「塔很重，所以基礎只需要考慮下壓，不會受拉。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The tower is heavy, so its foundation only needs to resist compression and never tension.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若節的開挖尺寸不足或被坍落土填塞，節的承壓貢獻大減，拉拔容量可能遠低於設計；放射狀連結若在施工縫處接合不良，三支腳柱的基礎無法共同作用，差異沉陷與傾斜風險增加。","textEn":"If knuckles are under-excavated or filled with collapsed soil, their bearing contribution drops sharply and uplift capacity can fall far below design; poor joints in the radial interconnection keep the three leg foundations from acting together, raising the risk of differential settlement and tilt.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「節狀連續壁樁的摩擦與拉拔」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Friction and uplift in knuckle wall piles\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若節的開挖尺寸不足或被坍落土填塞，節的承壓貢獻大減，拉拔容量可能遠低於設計；放射狀連結若在施工縫處接合不良，三支腳柱的基礎無法共同作用，差異沉陷與傾斜風險增加。","鋼構安裝只要每段都對準設計座標，量測時間不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","If knuckles are under-excavated or filled with collapsed soil, their bearing contribution drops sharply and uplift capacity can fall far below design.","As long as each segment is set to design coordinates, the time of surveying does not matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若節的開挖尺寸不足或被坍落土填塞，節的承壓貢獻大減，拉拔容量可能遠低於設計；放射狀連結若在施工縫處接合不良，三支腳柱的基礎無法共同作用，差異沉陷與傾斜風險增加。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If knuckles are under-excavated or filled with collapsed soil, their bearing contribution drops sharply and uplift capacity can fall far below design; poor joints in the radial interconnection keep the three leg foundations from acting together, raising the risk of differential settlement and tilt. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b024-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「細長塔身的日照彎曲與施工測量」與「在中央豎井內組裝並頂升天線塔」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Solar bowing and surveying a slender tower\" and \"Assembling and lifting the antenna mast inside the shaft\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b024-v13-17","title":"細長塔身的日照彎曲與施工測量：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Solar bowing and surveying a slender tower: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「日照彎曲與施工測量」如何影響東京晴空塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Solar bowing and construction survey” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tokyo Skytree”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"634 m 的細長鋼塔在日照下，向陽面鋼材升溫伸長、背陰面較冷，整個塔身會向背陽側彎曲，頂部偏移可達數十公分，並隨太陽方位在一天內移動。施工中每一段鋼管都要依座標安裝，若在日照強烈時測量並修正，等塔身冷卻後就會偏向另一側。因此測量必須在溫度均勻的時段（例如清晨）進行，或以溫度感測器即時修正，並把風造成的擺動另外扣除。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「日照彎曲與施工測量」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Under sunshine, a 634 m slender steel tower heats and lengthens on its sunny side while the shaded side stays cooler, so the whole body bows away from the sun with top movements that can reach tens of centimetres, shifting with the sun's bearing through the day. Every tube segment must be set to coordinates during erection, and surveying and correcting under strong sun leaves the tower leaning the other way once it cools. Surveys must therefore be done when temperatures are uniform, such as early morning, or corrected in real time with temperature sensors, with wind sway removed separately. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Solar bowing and construction survey” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：溫差彎曲頂部偏移 δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2B)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Top offset from thermal bowing δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2B).","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼構安裝只要每段都對準設計座標，量測時間不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"As long as each segment is set to design coordinates, the time of surveying does not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「日照彎曲與施工測量」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Solar bowing and construction survey”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-17-k1","title":"細長塔身的日照彎曲與施工測量","titleEn":"Solar bowing and surveying a slender tower","text":"634 m 的細長鋼塔在日照下，向陽面鋼材升溫伸長、背陰面較冷，整個塔身會向背陽側彎曲，頂部偏移可達數十公分，並隨太陽方位在一天內移動。施工中每一段鋼管都要依座標安裝，若在日照強烈時測量並修正，等塔身冷卻後就會偏向另一側。","textEn":"Under sunshine, a 634 m slender steel tower heats and lengthens on its sunny side while the shaded side stays cooler, so the whole body bows away from the sun with top movements that can reach tens of centimetres, shifting with the sun's bearing through the day. Every tube segment must be set to coordinates during erection, and surveying and correcting under strong sun leaves the tower leaning the other way once it cools.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼構安裝只要每段都對準設計座標，量測時間不重要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: As long as each segment is set to design coordinates, the time of surveying does not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「細長塔身的日照彎曲與施工測量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Solar bowing and surveying a slender tower\" is correct?","options":["鋼構安裝只要每段都對準設計座標，量測時間不重要。","在豎井內頂升比較安全，所以不需要另做結構分析。","634 m 的細長鋼塔在日照下，向陽面鋼材升溫伸長、背陰面較冷，整個塔身會向背陽側彎曲，頂部偏移可達數十公分，並隨太陽方位在一天內移動。"],"optionsEn":["As long as each segment is set to design coordinates, the time of surveying does not matter.","Lifting inside the shaft is safer, so no separate structural analysis is needed.","Under sunshine, a 634 m slender steel tower heats and lengthens on its sunny side while the shaded side stays cooler, so the whole body bows away from the sun with top movements that can reach tens of centimetres, shifting with the sun's bearing through the day."],"answer":2,"explanation":"634 m 的細長鋼塔在日照下，向陽面鋼材升溫伸長、背陰面較冷，整個塔身會向背陽側彎曲，頂部偏移可達數十公分，並隨太陽方位在一天內移動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Under sunshine, a 634 m slender steel tower heats and lengthens on its sunny side while the shaded side stays cooler, so the whole body bows away from the sun with top movements that can reach tens of centimetres, shifting with the sun's bearing through the day. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b024-v13-18","title":"細長塔身的日照彎曲與施工測量：定量估算","titleEn":"Solar bowing and surveying a slender tower: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「日照彎曲與施工測量」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Solar bowing and construction survey” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：溫差彎曲頂部偏移 δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2B)。α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C、兩側溫差 ΔT = 10 °C、施工高度 H = 400 m、該段寬度 B = 40 m，δ = 12×10⁻⁶×10×400²/(2×40) ≈ 0.24 m；溫差減為 3 °C 時偏移約 0.07 m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Top offset from thermal bowing δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2B). With α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C, a 10 °C difference across the section, a construction height H = 400 m and width B = 40 m, δ = 12×10⁻⁶×10×400²/(2×40) ≈ 0.24 m; at a 3 °C difference the offset is about 0.07 m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在塔身不同高度與方位設置溫度計與全球衛星定位接收器，建立溫差與頂部偏移的關係；每段鋼構安裝後於清晨無風時複測座標，與施工階段分析預測的形狀（含自重與溫度）比較，確認偏差在容許範圍內才可進行下一段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Install thermometers and satellite-positioning receivers at several heights and orientations to correlate temperature difference with top offset; after each segment is erected, resurvey coordinates in calm early-morning conditions and compare with the shape predicted by construction-stage analysis including self-weight and temperature, proceeding only when deviations are within tolerance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"溫差彎曲頂部偏移 δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2B)。α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C、兩側溫差 ΔT = 10 °C、施工高度 H = 400 m、該段寬度 B = 40 m，δ = 12×10⁻⁶×10×400²/(2×40) ≈ 0.24 m；溫差減為 3 °C 時偏移約 0.07 m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Top offset from thermal bowing δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2B). With α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C, a 10 °C difference across the section, a construction height H = 400 m and width B = 40 m, δ = 12×10⁻⁶×10×400²/(2×40) ≈ 0.24 m; at a 3 °C difference the offset is about 0.07 m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「細長塔身的日照彎曲與施工測量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Solar bowing and surveying a slender tower\", which statement holds?","options":["溫差彎曲頂部偏移 δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2B)。","地震後只要外觀沒有明顯損壞，施工中的結構就可以立即復工。","主鋼管很厚，所以腐蝕對鋼管塔沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Top offset from thermal bowing δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2B).","If there is no visible damage after an earthquake, work on an unfinished structure can resume immediately.","The main tubes are very thick, so corrosion does not matter for a tube tower."],"answer":0,"explanation":"溫差彎曲頂部偏移 δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2B)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Top offset from thermal bowing δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2B). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b024-v13-19","title":"細長塔身的日照彎曲與施工測量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Solar bowing and surveying a slender tower: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「日照彎曲與施工測量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Solar bowing and construction survey” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在塔身不同高度與方位設置溫度計與全球衛星定位接收器，建立溫差與頂部偏移的關係；每段鋼構安裝後於清晨無風時複測座標，與施工階段分析預測的形狀（含自重與溫度）比較，確認偏差在容許範圍內才可進行下一段。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Install thermometers and satellite-positioning receivers at several heights and orientations to correlate temperature difference with top offset; after each segment is erected, resurvey coordinates in calm early-morning conditions and compare with the shape predicted by construction-stage analysis including self-weight and temperature, proceeding only when deviations are within tolerance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：測量程序書要規定量測時段、溫差上限與風速上限，所有修正量由測量主管與結構工程師共同核可；三支腳柱必須在同一時段量測，資料保留以供日後完工形狀比對。","observationEn":"Site practice: The survey procedure fixes measurement windows, maximum temperature difference and maximum wind speed, with all corrections approved jointly by the survey lead and the structural engineer; survey the three legs in the same window and keep the data for later comparison with the as-built shape.","failure":"注意干擾：若在午後量測並依此修正，塔身冷卻後會偏離設計軸線，累積到上部時天線塔可能無法對準中央豎井；三支腳柱若各自以不同時段的測量資料修正，塔身會出現扭轉誤差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Correcting from afternoon surveys leaves the tower off its design axis once it cools, and by the upper levels the antenna mast may no longer align with the central shaft; correcting each of the three legs from surveys taken at different times introduces a twist error into the tower. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在塔身不同高度與方位設置溫度計與全球衛星定位接收器，建立溫差與頂部偏移的關係；每段鋼構安裝後於清晨無風時複測座標，與施工階段分析預測的形狀（含自重與溫度）比較，確認偏差在容許範圍內才可進行下一段。","textEn":"Install thermometers and satellite-positioning receivers at several heights and orientations to correlate temperature difference with top offset; after each segment is erected, resurvey coordinates in calm early-morning conditions and compare with the shape predicted by construction-stage analysis including self-weight and temperature, proceeding only when deviations are within tolerance.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"測量程序書要規定量測時段、溫差上限與風速上限，所有修正量由測量主管與結構工程師共同核可；三支腳柱必須在同一時段量測，資料保留以供日後完工形狀比對。","textEn":"The survey procedure fixes measurement windows, maximum temperature difference and maximum wind speed, with all corrections approved jointly by the survey lead and the structural engineer; survey the three legs in the same window and keep the data for later comparison with the as-built shape.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「細長塔身的日照彎曲與施工測量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Solar bowing and surveying a slender tower\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在塔身不同高度與方位設置溫度計與全球衛星定位接收器，建立溫差與頂部偏移的關係。","心柱是用來支撐鋼塔重量的主柱。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Install thermometers and satellite-positioning receivers at several heights and orientations to correlate temperature difference with top offset.","The central column is the main column that carries the steel tower's weight."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在塔身不同高度與方位設置溫度計與全球衛星定位接收器，建立溫差與頂部偏移的關係；每段鋼構安裝後於清晨無風時複測座標，與施工階段分析預測的形狀（含自重與溫度）比較，確認偏差在容許範圍內才可進行下一段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Install thermometers and satellite-positioning receivers at several heights and orientations to correlate temperature difference with top offset; after each segment is erected, resurvey coordinates in calm early-morning conditions and compare with the shape predicted by construction-stage analysis including self-weight and temperature, proceeding only when deviations are within tolerance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b024-v13-20","title":"細長塔身的日照彎曲與施工測量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Solar bowing and surveying a slender tower: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「日照彎曲與施工測量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Solar bowing and construction survey” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若在午後量測並依此修正，塔身冷卻後會偏離設計軸線，累積到上部時天線塔可能無法對準中央豎井；三支腳柱若各自以不同時段的測量資料修正，塔身會出現扭轉誤差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Correcting from afternoon surveys leaves the tower off its design axis once it cools, and by the upper levels the antenna mast may no longer align with the central shaft; correcting each of the three legs from surveys taken at different times introduces a twist error into the tower. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此測量必須在溫度均勻的時段（例如清晨）進行，或以溫度感測器即時修正，並把風造成的擺動另外扣除。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Surveys must therefore be done when temperatures are uniform, such as early morning, or corrected in real time with temperature sensors, with wind sway removed separately.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼構安裝只要每段都對準設計座標，量測時間不重要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"As long as each segment is set to design coordinates, the time of surveying does not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若在午後量測並依此修正，塔身冷卻後會偏離設計軸線，累積到上部時天線塔可能無法對準中央豎井；三支腳柱若各自以不同時段的測量資料修正，塔身會出現扭轉誤差。","textEn":"Correcting from afternoon surveys leaves the tower off its design axis once it cools, and by the upper levels the antenna mast may no longer align with the central shaft; correcting each of the three legs from surveys taken at different times introduces a twist error into the tower.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「細長塔身的日照彎曲與施工測量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Solar bowing and surveying a slender tower\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","在豎井內頂升比較安全，所以不需要另做結構分析。","若在午後量測並依此修正，塔身冷卻後會偏離設計軸線，累積到上部時天線塔可能無法對準中央豎井；三支腳柱若各自以不同時段的測量資料修正，塔身會出現扭轉誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Lifting inside the shaft is safer, so no separate structural analysis is needed.","Correcting from afternoon surveys leaves the tower off its design axis once it cools, and by the upper levels the antenna mast may no longer align with the central shaft."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若在午後量測並依此修正，塔身冷卻後會偏離設計軸線，累積到上部時天線塔可能無法對準中央豎井；三支腳柱若各自以不同時段的測量資料修正，塔身會出現扭轉誤差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Correcting from afternoon surveys leaves the tower off its design axis once it cools, and by the upper levels the antenna mast may no longer align with the central shaft; correcting each of the three legs from surveys taken at different times introduces a twist error into the tower. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b024-v13-21","title":"在中央豎井內組裝並頂升天線塔：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Assembling and lifting the antenna mast inside the shaft: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「天線塔頂升」如何影響東京晴空塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gain-tower lift-up” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tokyo Skytree”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"晴空塔頂部的天線塔（gain tower）外徑約 6 m，並未用塔吊一節一節吊到 600 m 以上，而是在塔身中央的豎井內由下往上組裝，連同避雷設施與兩組合計約 100 公噸的調諧質量阻尼器，逐段頂升推出塔頂。2010 年 12 月開始在豎井內逐步上推，2011 年 3 月達到 634 m。豎井內頂升避免了在極高處以塔吊吊裝大型構件，也讓高空作業轉移到有遮蔽的豎井內；代價是頂升期間塔身要承受天線塔的移動荷重與導引反力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「天線塔頂升」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The antenna mast, or gain tower, at the top of Skytree is about 6 m in outside diameter. Rather than being lifted piece by piece by crane above 600 m, it was assembled inside the central shaft from below and jacked upward in stages, carrying lightning protection and two tuned mass dampers totalling about 100 t, until it emerged at the top. Lifting inside the shaft began in December 2010 and the mast reached 634 m in March 2011. Lifting within the shaft avoided crane lifts of large members at extreme height and moved work at height into a sheltered shaft, at the cost of the tower carrying the mast's moving load and guide reactions during the lift. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Gain-tower lift-up” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：頂升荷重分配：若天線塔連同附屬設備重 3,000 t，W = 3,000×9.81 ≈ 29.4 MN，由 6 具千斤頂分擔各約 4.9 MN；計入 1.25 動力與不均勻係數後約 6.1 MN，選用 8 MN 千斤頂時使用率約 77%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Jacking load sharing: if the mast with its equipment weighs 3,000 t, W = 3,000×9.81 ≈ 29.4 MN, about 4.9 MN on each of 6 jacks; with a 1.25 factor for dynamics and unevenness this is about 6.1 MN, a utilisation of about 77% on 8 MN jacks.","failure":"常見誤解：「在豎井內頂升比較安全，所以不需要另做結構分析。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lifting inside the shaft is safer, so no separate structural analysis is needed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「天線塔頂升」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Gain-tower lift-up”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-21-k1","title":"在中央豎井內組裝並頂升天線塔","titleEn":"Assembling and lifting the antenna mast inside the shaft","text":"晴空塔頂部的天線塔（gain tower）外徑約 6 m，並未用塔吊一節一節吊到 600 m 以上，而是在塔身中央的豎井內由下往上組裝，連同避雷設施與兩組合計約 100 公噸的調諧質量阻尼器，逐段頂升推出塔頂。2010 年 12 月開始在豎井內逐步上推，2011 年 3 月達到 634 m。","textEn":"The antenna mast, or gain tower, at the top of Skytree is about 6 m in outside diameter. Rather than being lifted piece by piece by crane above 600 m, it was assembled inside the central shaft from below and jacked upward in stages, carrying lightning protection and two tuned mass dampers totalling about 100 t, until it emerged at the top.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：在豎井內頂升比較安全，所以不需要另做結構分析。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lifting inside the shaft is safer, so no separate structural analysis is needed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「在中央豎井內組裝並頂升天線塔」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Assembling and lifting the antenna mast inside the shaft\" is correct?","options":["晴空塔頂部的天線塔（gain tower）外徑約 6 m，並未用塔吊一節一節吊到 600 m 以上，而是在塔身中央的豎井內由下往上組裝，連同避雷設施與兩組合計約 100 公噸的調諧質量阻尼器，逐段頂升推出塔頂。","在豎井內頂升比較安全，所以不需要另做結構分析。","阻尼器的力量越大越好，不需要限制。"],"optionsEn":["The antenna mast, or gain tower, at the top of Skytree is about 6 m in outside diameter.","Lifting inside the shaft is safer, so no separate structural analysis is needed.","The larger a damper's force the better, so it needs no limit."],"answer":0,"explanation":"晴空塔頂部的天線塔（gain tower）外徑約 6 m，並未用塔吊一節一節吊到 600 m 以上，而是在塔身中央的豎井內由下往上組裝，連同避雷設施與兩組合計約 100 公噸的調諧質量阻尼器，逐段頂升推出塔頂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The antenna mast, or gain tower, at the top of Skytree is about 6 m in outside diameter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b024-v13-22","title":"在中央豎井內組裝並頂升天線塔：定量估算","titleEn":"Assembling and lifting the antenna mast inside the shaft: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「天線塔頂升」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gain-tower lift-up” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：頂升荷重分配：若天線塔連同附屬設備重 3,000 t，W = 3,000×9.81 ≈ 29.4 MN，由 6 具千斤頂分擔各約 4.9 MN；計入 1.25 動力與不均勻係數後約 6.1 MN，選用 8 MN 千斤頂時使用率約 77%。若行程 0.5 m、需推升 130 m，約 260 個循環。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Jacking load sharing: if the mast with its equipment weighs 3,000 t, W = 3,000×9.81 ≈ 29.4 MN, about 4.9 MN on each of 6 jacks; with a 1.25 factor for dynamics and unevenness this is about 6.1 MN, a utilisation of about 77% on 8 MN jacks. With a 0.5 m stroke, a 130 m lift needs about 260 cycles. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：頂升前以施工階段分析檢查各頂升位置時塔身的應力與變形，千斤頂壓力以同步控制系統即時監測，各點荷重差異超過設定值即停止；每次頂升後量測天線塔的垂直度與導引間隙，並在強風預報時停止頂升並鎖定。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before jacking, check tower stresses and deformation at each lift position with construction-stage analysis, monitor jack pressures in real time through a synchronised control system, and stop when load differences between points exceed the set value; after each lift measure mast verticality and guide clearances, stopping and locking whenever strong winds are forecast.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"頂升荷重分配：若天線塔連同附屬設備重 3,000 t，W = 3,000×9.81 ≈ 29.4 MN，由 6 具千斤頂分擔各約 4.9 MN；計入 1.25 動力與不均勻係數後約 6.1 MN，選用 8 MN 千斤頂時使用率約 77%。若行程 0.5 m、需推升 130 m，約 260 個循環。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Jacking load sharing: if the mast with its equipment weighs 3,000 t, W = 3,000×9.81 ≈ 29.4 MN, about 4.9 MN on each of 6 jacks; with a 1.25 factor for dynamics and unevenness this is about 6.1 MN, a utilisation of about 77% on 8 MN jacks. With a 0.5 m stroke, a 130 m lift needs about 260 cycles. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「在中央豎井內組裝並頂升天線塔」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Assembling and lifting the antenna mast inside the shaft\", which statement holds?","options":["落冰只是維護清潔問題，和結構工程無關。","頂升荷重分配：若天線塔連同附屬設備重 3,000 t，W = 3,000×9.81 ≈ 29.4 MN，由 6 具千斤頂分擔各約 4.9 MN。","格構塔透風，所以風力可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Falling ice is only a cleaning issue and has nothing to do with structural engineering.","Jacking load sharing: if the mast with its equipment weighs 3,000 t, W = 3,000×9.81 ≈ 29.4 MN, about 4.9 MN on each of 6 jacks.","A lattice tower lets the wind through, so wind force can be ignored."],"answer":1,"explanation":"頂升荷重分配：若天線塔連同附屬設備重 3,000 t，W = 3,000×9.81 ≈ 29.4 MN，由 6 具千斤頂分擔各約 4.9 MN；計入 1.25 動力與不均勻係數後約 6.1 MN，選用 8 MN 千斤頂時使用率約 77%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Jacking load sharing: if the mast with its equipment weighs 3,000 t, W = 3,000×9.81 ≈ 29.4 MN, about 4.9 MN on each of 6 jacks; with a 1.25 factor for dynamics and unevenness this is about 6.1 MN, a utilisation of about 77% on 8 MN jacks. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b024-v13-23","title":"在中央豎井內組裝並頂升天線塔：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Assembling and lifting the antenna mast inside the shaft: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「天線塔頂升」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gain-tower lift-up” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"頂升前以施工階段分析檢查各頂升位置時塔身的應力與變形，千斤頂壓力以同步控制系統即時監測，各點荷重差異超過設定值即停止；每次頂升後量測天線塔的垂直度與導引間隙，並在強風預報時停止頂升並鎖定。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before jacking, check tower stresses and deformation at each lift position with construction-stage analysis, monitor jack pressures in real time through a synchronised control system, and stop when load differences between points exceed the set value; after each lift measure mast verticality and guide clearances, stopping and locking whenever strong winds are forecast. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：頂升計畫要列出每一段的荷重、千斤頂壓力上限、同步誤差容許值、風速停工條件與鎖定程序；每次頂升開始前設停止點，由頂升工程師與結構工程師共同確認後才可啟動。","observationEn":"Site practice: The lifting plan lists the load at each stage, jack-pressure limits, allowable synchronisation error, wind stop limits and locking procedure; set a hold point before every lift so it starts only after the lifting engineer and structural engineer jointly confirm.","failure":"注意干擾：若各千斤頂不同步，天線塔會傾斜並卡在導引上，造成導引構件與塔身局部超載；頂升中遭遇強風而未鎖定時，部分伸出的天線塔像懸臂受風，根部彎矩可能超過臨時支承的容量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the jacks fall out of sync, the mast tilts and jams in its guides, locally overloading guide members and the tower; if it is not locked when strong wind arrives mid-lift, the partly extended mast acts as a cantilever in the wind and its root moment can exceed the temporary supports' capacity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"頂升前以施工階段分析檢查各頂升位置時塔身的應力與變形，千斤頂壓力以同步控制系統即時監測，各點荷重差異超過設定值即停止；每次頂升後量測天線塔的垂直度與導引間隙，並在強風預報時停止頂升並鎖定。","textEn":"Before jacking, check tower stresses and deformation at each lift position with construction-stage analysis, monitor jack pressures in real time through a synchronised control system, and stop when load differences between points exceed the set value; after each lift measure mast verticality and guide clearances, stopping and locking whenever strong winds are forecast.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"頂升計畫要列出每一段的荷重、千斤頂壓力上限、同步誤差容許值、風速停工條件與鎖定程序；每次頂升開始前設停止點，由頂升工程師與結構工程師共同確認後才可啟動。","textEn":"The lifting plan lists the load at each stage, jack-pressure limits, allowable synchronisation error, wind stop limits and locking procedure; set a hold point before every lift so it starts only after the lifting engineer and structural engineer jointly confirm.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「在中央豎井內組裝並頂升天線塔」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Assembling and lifting the antenna mast inside the shaft\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","鋼管越粗越厚就越安全，接頭細節不重要。","頂升前以施工階段分析檢查各頂升位置時塔身的應力與變形，千斤頂壓力以同步控制系統即時監測，各點荷重差異超過設定值即停止。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The bigger and thicker the tube, the safer it is; joint details do not matter.","Before jacking, check tower stresses and deformation at each lift position with construction-stage analysis, monitor jack pressures in real time through a synchronised control system, and stop when load differences between points exceed the set value."],"answer":2,"explanation":"頂升前以施工階段分析檢查各頂升位置時塔身的應力與變形，千斤頂壓力以同步控制系統即時監測，各點荷重差異超過設定值即停止；每次頂升後量測天線塔的垂直度與導引間隙，並在強風預報時停止頂升並鎖定。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before jacking, check tower stresses and deformation at each lift position with construction-stage analysis, monitor jack pressures in real time through a synchronised control system, and stop when load differences between points exceed the set value; after each lift measure mast verticality and guide clearances, stopping and locking whenever strong winds are forecast. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b024-v13-24","title":"在中央豎井內組裝並頂升天線塔：失效診斷","titleEn":"Assembling and lifting the antenna mast inside the shaft: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「天線塔頂升」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gain-tower lift-up” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若各千斤頂不同步，天線塔會傾斜並卡在導引上，造成導引構件與塔身局部超載；頂升中遭遇強風而未鎖定時，部分伸出的天線塔像懸臂受風，根部彎矩可能超過臨時支承的容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the jacks fall out of sync, the mast tilts and jams in its guides, locally overloading guide members and the tower; if it is not locked when strong wind arrives mid-lift, the partly extended mast acts as a cantilever in the wind and its root moment can exceed the temporary supports' capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：豎井內頂升避免了在極高處以塔吊吊裝大型構件，也讓高空作業轉移到有遮蔽的豎井內；代價是頂升期間塔身要承受天線塔的移動荷重與導引反力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Lifting within the shaft avoided crane lifts of large members at extreme height and moved work at height into a sheltered shaft, at the cost of the tower carrying the mast's moving load and guide reactions during the lift.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「在豎井內頂升比較安全，所以不需要另做結構分析。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lifting inside the shaft is safer, so no separate structural analysis is needed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若各千斤頂不同步，天線塔會傾斜並卡在導引上，造成導引構件與塔身局部超載；頂升中遭遇強風而未鎖定時，部分伸出的天線塔像懸臂受風，根部彎矩可能超過臨時支承的容量。","textEn":"If the jacks fall out of sync, the mast tilts and jams in its guides, locally overloading guide members and the tower; if it is not locked when strong wind arrives mid-lift, the partly extended mast acts as a cantilever in the wind and its root moment can exceed the temporary supports' capacity.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「在中央豎井內組裝並頂升天線塔」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Assembling and lifting the antenna mast inside the shaft\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若各千斤頂不同步，天線塔會傾斜並卡在導引上，造成導引構件與塔身局部超載；頂升中遭遇強風而未鎖定時，部分伸出的天線塔像懸臂受風，根部彎矩可能超過臨時支承的容量。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","阻尼器的力量越大越好，不需要限制。"],"optionsEn":["If the jacks fall out of sync, the mast tilts and jams in its guides, locally overloading guide members and the tower.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","The larger a damper's force the better, so it needs no limit."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若各千斤頂不同步，天線塔會傾斜並卡在導引上，造成導引構件與塔身局部超載；頂升中遭遇強風而未鎖定時，部分伸出的天線塔像懸臂受風，根部彎矩可能超過臨時支承的容量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the jacks fall out of sync, the mast tilts and jams in its guides, locally overloading guide members and the tower; if it is not locked when strong wind arrives mid-lift, the partly extended mast acts as a cantilever in the wind and its root moment can exceed the temporary supports' capacity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b024-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「心柱油壓阻尼器的性能驗證」與「2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Verifying the central-column oil dampers\" and \"Inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b024-v13-25","title":"心柱油壓阻尼器的性能驗證：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Verifying the central-column oil dampers: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「油壓阻尼器的雙線性特性」如何影響東京晴空塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bilinear oil-damper behaviour” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tokyo Skytree”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"連接心柱與鋼塔的油壓阻尼器必須在中小振動時提供足夠阻尼，又不能在大地震時產生過大的力而損壞心柱或鋼塔接頭。常見做法是加裝釋壓閥，使阻尼器呈雙線性：速度低於某一門檻時阻尼力與速度成正比，超過門檻後阻尼係數大幅降低，力量只緩慢增加。驗證的重點是確認實際產品的門檻速度、兩段阻尼係數與溫度影響，與分析模型使用的參數一致。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「油壓阻尼器的雙線性特性」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The oil dampers linking the central column and steel tower must provide enough damping in small and moderate vibrations without generating forces large enough in a major earthquake to damage the column or tower connections. A common solution is a relief valve that makes the damper bilinear: below a threshold velocity force is proportional to velocity, and above it the damping coefficient drops sharply so force rises only slowly. Verification focuses on confirming that the actual units' threshold velocity, two damping coefficients and temperature sensitivity match the parameters used in the analysis model. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Bilinear oil-damper behaviour” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：雙線性阻尼 F = c₁·v（v ≤ v_r），F = c₁·v_r + c₂·(v − v_r)（v > v_r）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Bilinear damping: F = c₁·v for v ≤ v_r and F = c₁·v_r + c₂·(v − v_r) for v > v_r.","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器的力量越大越好，不需要限制。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The larger a damper's force the better, so it needs no limit.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「油壓阻尼器的雙線性特性」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Bilinear oil-damper behaviour”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-25-k1","title":"心柱油壓阻尼器的性能驗證","titleEn":"Verifying the central-column oil dampers","text":"連接心柱與鋼塔的油壓阻尼器必須在中小振動時提供足夠阻尼，又不能在大地震時產生過大的力而損壞心柱或鋼塔接頭。常見做法是加裝釋壓閥，使阻尼器呈雙線性：速度低於某一門檻時阻尼力與速度成正比，超過門檻後阻尼係數大幅降低，力量只緩慢增加。","textEn":"The oil dampers linking the central column and steel tower must provide enough damping in small and moderate vibrations without generating forces large enough in a major earthquake to damage the column or tower connections. A common solution is a relief valve that makes the damper bilinear: below a threshold velocity force is proportional to velocity, and above it the damping coefficient drops sharply so force rises only slowly.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器的力量越大越好，不需要限制。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The larger a damper's force the better, so it needs no limit. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「心柱油壓阻尼器的性能驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Verifying the central-column oil dampers\" is correct?","options":["阻尼器的力量越大越好，不需要限制。","連接心柱與鋼塔的油壓阻尼器必須在中小振動時提供足夠阻尼，又不能在大地震時產生過大的力而損壞心柱或鋼塔接頭。","地震後只要外觀沒有明顯損壞，施工中的結構就可以立即復工。"],"optionsEn":["The larger a damper's force the better, so it needs no limit.","The oil dampers linking the central column and steel tower must provide enough damping in small and moderate vibrations without generating forces large enough in a major earthquake to damage the column or tower connections.","If there is no visible damage after an earthquake, work on an unfinished structure can resume immediately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"連接心柱與鋼塔的油壓阻尼器必須在中小振動時提供足夠阻尼，又不能在大地震時產生過大的力而損壞心柱或鋼塔接頭。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The oil dampers linking the central column and steel tower must provide enough damping in small and moderate vibrations without generating forces large enough in a major earthquake to damage the column or tower connections. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b024-v13-26","title":"心柱油壓阻尼器的性能驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Verifying the central-column oil dampers: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「油壓阻尼器的雙線性特性」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bilinear oil-damper behaviour” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：雙線性阻尼 F = c₁·v（v ≤ v_r），F = c₁·v_r + c₂·(v − v_r)（v > v_r）。取 c₁ = 10,000 kN·s/m、v_r = 0.1 m/s、c₂ = 1,000 kN·s/m：v = 0.3 m/s 時 F = 1,000 + 1,000×0.2 = 1,200 kN，若無釋壓閥則為 3,000 kN，接頭設計力可降低六成。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Bilinear damping: F = c₁·v for v ≤ v_r and F = c₁·v_r + c₂·(v − v_r) for v > v_r. With c₁ = 10,000 kN·s/m, v_r = 0.1 m/s and c₂ = 1,000 kN·s/m, at v = 0.3 m/s F = 1,000 + 1,000×0.2 = 1,200 kN, versus 3,000 kN without a relief valve, cutting the connection design force by 60%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每一具阻尼器出廠前以動態試驗機做正弦加載，涵蓋門檻速度上下的多個速度與溫度，繪出力—速度曲線並與規格允差比較；安裝後檢查固定端螺栓預力、油位與行程指示，並把序號與試驗結果對應存檔。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before delivery, test every damper on a dynamic rig with sinusoidal loading at several velocities above and below the threshold and at several temperatures, plotting force–velocity curves against the specified tolerance; after installation check end-connection bolt preload, oil level and stroke indicators, and file serial numbers against test results.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"雙線性阻尼 F = c₁·v（v ≤ v_r），F = c₁·v_r + c₂·(v − v_r)（v > v_r）。取 c₁ = 10,000 kN·s/m、v_r = 0.1 m/s、c₂ = 1,000 kN·s/m：v = 0.3 m/s 時 F = 1,000 + 1,000×0.2 = 1,200 kN，若無釋壓閥則為 3,000 kN，接頭設計力可降低六成。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Bilinear damping: F = c₁·v for v ≤ v_r and F = c₁·v_r + c₂·(v − v_r) for v > v_r. With c₁ = 10,000 kN·s/m, v_r = 0.1 m/s and c₂ = 1,000 kN·s/m, at v = 0.3 m/s F = 1,000 + 1,000×0.2 = 1,200 kN, versus 3,000 kN without a relief valve, cutting the connection design force by 60%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「心柱油壓阻尼器的性能驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Verifying the central-column oil dampers\", which statement holds?","options":["主鋼管很厚，所以腐蝕對鋼管塔沒有影響。","心柱是用來支撐鋼塔重量的主柱。","雙線性阻尼 F = c₁·v（v ≤ v_r），F = c₁·v_r + c₂·(v − v_r)（v > v_r）。"],"optionsEn":["The main tubes are very thick, so corrosion does not matter for a tube tower.","The central column is the main column that carries the steel tower's weight.","Bilinear damping: F = c₁·v for v ≤ v_r and F = c₁·v_r + c₂·(v − v_r) for v > v_r."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雙線性阻尼 F = c₁·v（v ≤ v_r），F = c₁·v_r + c₂·(v − v_r)（v > v_r）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Bilinear damping: F = c₁·v for v ≤ v_r and F = c₁·v_r + c₂·(v − v_r) for v > v_r. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b024-v13-27","title":"心柱油壓阻尼器的性能驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Verifying the central-column oil dampers: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「油壓阻尼器的雙線性特性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bilinear oil-damper behaviour” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每一具阻尼器出廠前以動態試驗機做正弦加載，涵蓋門檻速度上下的多個速度與溫度，繪出力—速度曲線並與規格允差比較；安裝後檢查固定端螺栓預力、油位與行程指示，並把序號與試驗結果對應存檔。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before delivery, test every damper on a dynamic rig with sinusoidal loading at several velocities above and below the threshold and at several temperatures, plotting force–velocity curves against the specified tolerance; after installation check end-connection bolt preload, oil level and stroke indicators, and file serial numbers against test results. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：採購規範要寫明門檻速度、兩段阻尼係數、溫度範圍內的變化上限與逐具試驗要求；心柱與鋼塔接頭的設計力須以阻尼器可能的最大力（含製造允差）計算，並由結構設計者確認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The procurement specification states the threshold velocity, both damping coefficients, the maximum variation over the temperature range and unit-by-unit testing; design the column and tower connections for the damper's maximum possible force including manufacturing tolerance, confirmed by the structural designer.","failure":"注意干擾：釋壓閥設定過高時，大地震中阻尼器力量超出接頭容量，可能拉壞心柱的埋件；設定過低則中小地震時阻尼不足，心柱制振效果打折。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A relief valve set too high lets damper force exceed connection capacity in a major earthquake, possibly tearing out embeds in the column; set too low, it leaves too little damping in moderate earthquakes and weakens the central-column scheme. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每一具阻尼器出廠前以動態試驗機做正弦加載，涵蓋門檻速度上下的多個速度與溫度，繪出力—速度曲線並與規格允差比較；安裝後檢查固定端螺栓預力、油位與行程指示，並把序號與試驗結果對應存檔。","textEn":"Before delivery, test every damper on a dynamic rig with sinusoidal loading at several velocities above and below the threshold and at several temperatures, plotting force–velocity curves against the specified tolerance; after installation check end-connection bolt preload, oil level and stroke indicators, and file serial numbers against test results.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"採購規範要寫明門檻速度、兩段阻尼係數、溫度範圍內的變化上限與逐具試驗要求；心柱與鋼塔接頭的設計力須以阻尼器可能的最大力（含製造允差）計算，並由結構設計者確認。","textEn":"The procurement specification states the threshold velocity, both damping coefficients, the maximum variation over the temperature range and unit-by-unit testing; design the column and tower connections for the damper's maximum possible force including manufacturing tolerance, confirmed by the structural designer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「心柱油壓阻尼器的性能驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Verifying the central-column oil dampers\"?","options":["每一具阻尼器出廠前以動態試驗機做正弦加載，涵蓋門檻速度上下的多個速度與溫度，繪出力—速度曲線並與規格允差比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","塔很重，所以基礎只需要考慮下壓，不會受拉。"],"optionsEn":["Before delivery, test every damper on a dynamic rig with sinusoidal loading at several velocities above and below the threshold and at several temperatures, plotting force–velocity curves against the specified tolerance.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The tower is heavy, so its foundation only needs to resist compression and never tension."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每一具阻尼器出廠前以動態試驗機做正弦加載，涵蓋門檻速度上下的多個速度與溫度，繪出力—速度曲線並與規格允差比較；安裝後檢查固定端螺栓預力、油位與行程指示，並把序號與試驗結果對應存檔。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before delivery, test every damper on a dynamic rig with sinusoidal loading at several velocities above and below the threshold and at several temperatures, plotting force–velocity curves against the specified tolerance; after installation check end-connection bolt preload, oil level and stroke indicators, and file serial numbers against test results. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b024-v13-28","title":"心柱油壓阻尼器的性能驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Verifying the central-column oil dampers: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「油壓阻尼器的雙線性特性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bilinear oil-damper behaviour” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"釋壓閥設定過高時，大地震中阻尼器力量超出接頭容量，可能拉壞心柱的埋件；設定過低則中小地震時阻尼不足，心柱制振效果打折。密封老化漏油會使兩段阻尼係數同時下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A relief valve set too high lets damper force exceed connection capacity in a major earthquake, possibly tearing out embeds in the column; set too low, it leaves too little damping in moderate earthquakes and weakens the central-column scheme. Ageing seals that leak oil lower both damping coefficients. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：驗證的重點是確認實際產品的門檻速度、兩段阻尼係數與溫度影響，與分析模型使用的參數一致。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Verification focuses on confirming that the actual units' threshold velocity, two damping coefficients and temperature sensitivity match the parameters used in the analysis model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器的力量越大越好，不需要限制。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The larger a damper's force the better, so it needs no limit.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"釋壓閥設定過高時，大地震中阻尼器力量超出接頭容量，可能拉壞心柱的埋件；設定過低則中小地震時阻尼不足，心柱制振效果打折。密封老化漏油會使兩段阻尼係數同時下降。","textEn":"A relief valve set too high lets damper force exceed connection capacity in a major earthquake, possibly tearing out embeds in the column; set too low, it leaves too little damping in moderate earthquakes and weakens the central-column scheme. Ageing seals that leak oil lower both damping coefficients.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「心柱油壓阻尼器的性能驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Verifying the central-column oil dampers\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","釋壓閥設定過高時，大地震中阻尼器力量超出接頭容量，可能拉壞心柱的埋件；設定過低則中小地震時阻尼不足，心柱制振效果打折。","地震後只要外觀沒有明顯損壞，施工中的結構就可以立即復工。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A relief valve set too high lets damper force exceed connection capacity in a major earthquake, possibly tearing out embeds in the column.","If there is no visible damage after an earthquake, work on an unfinished structure can resume immediately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"釋壓閥設定過高時，大地震中阻尼器力量超出接頭容量，可能拉壞心柱的埋件；設定過低則中小地震時阻尼不足，心柱制振效果打折。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A relief valve set too high lets damper force exceed connection capacity in a major earthquake, possibly tearing out embeds in the column; set too low, it leaves too little damping in moderate earthquakes and weakens the central-column scheme. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b024-v13-29","title":"2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「施工中強震後檢查」如何影響東京晴空塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Post-earthquake inspection during construction” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tokyo Skytree”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"2011 年 3 月 11 日東北地方太平洋近海地震發生時，晴空塔已接近完成高度，天線塔仍在頂升階段；地震後塔體接受全面檢查，業主公開表示人員安全、結構無損，一週後的 3 月 18 日達到 634 m。施工中的結構與完工狀態不同：阻尼器可能尚未全部連接、臨時支承仍在、上部有移動中的構件，因此地震後的檢查必須以當時的施工狀態為基準，而不是以完工設計為基準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「施工中強震後檢查」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When the Tōhoku earthquake struck on 11 March 2011, Skytree was close to full height with the antenna mast still being lifted; the tower was fully inspected afterwards, the owner announced that workers were safe and the structure undamaged, and it reached 634 m a week later on 18 March. A structure under construction differs from the finished state: dampers may not all be connected, temporary supports remain and members at the top may be in motion, so post-earthquake inspection must be based on the construction state at the time, not on the completed design. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Post-earthquake inspection during construction” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：殘留傾斜判斷：比較地震前後同一時段、相近溫度下的頂部座標，若差值 12 mm、量測高度 600 m，傾角 12/600,000 = 1/50,000；若量測不確定度為 ±15 mm，差值小於兩倍不確定度，可判定沒有可量測的殘留變形。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Residual tilt check: compare top coordinates before and after the earthquake at the same time of day and similar temperature; a 12 mm difference at 600 m is a tilt of 12/600,000 = 1/50,000, and with a survey uncertainty of ±15 mm the change is below twice the uncertainty, so no measurable residual deformation is concluded.","failure":"常見誤解：「地震後只要外觀沒有明顯損壞，施工中的結構就可以立即復工。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If there is no visible damage after an earthquake, work on an unfinished structure can resume immediately.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「施工中強震後檢查」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Post-earthquake inspection during construction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-29-k1","title":"2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查","titleEn":"Inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake","text":"2011 年 3 月 11 日東北地方太平洋近海地震發生時，晴空塔已接近完成高度，天線塔仍在頂升階段；地震後塔體接受全面檢查，業主公開表示人員安全、結構無損，一週後的 3 月 18 日達到 634 m。施工中的結構與完工狀態不同：阻尼器可能尚未全部連接、臨時支承仍在、上部有移動中的構件，因此地震後的檢查必須以當時的施工狀態為基準，而不是以完工設計為基準。","textEn":"When the Tōhoku earthquake struck on 11 March 2011, Skytree was close to full height with the antenna mast still being lifted; the tower was fully inspected afterwards, the owner announced that workers were safe and the structure undamaged, and it reached 634 m a week later on 18 March. A structure under construction differs from the finished state: dampers may not all be connected, temporary supports remain and members at the top may be in motion, so post-earthquake inspection must be based on the construction state at the time, not on the completed design.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地震後只要外觀沒有明顯損壞，施工中的結構就可以立即復工。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If there is no visible damage after an earthquake, work on an unfinished structure can resume immediately. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake\" is correct?","options":["地震後只要外觀沒有明顯損壞，施工中的結構就可以立即復工。","落冰只是維護清潔問題，和結構工程無關。","2011 年 3 月 11 日東北地方太平洋近海地震發生時，晴空塔已接近完成高度，天線塔仍在頂升階段。"],"optionsEn":["If there is no visible damage after an earthquake, work on an unfinished structure can resume immediately.","Falling ice is only a cleaning issue and has nothing to do with structural engineering.","When the Tōhoku earthquake struck on 11 March 2011, Skytree was close to full height with the antenna mast still being lifted."],"answer":2,"explanation":"2011 年 3 月 11 日東北地方太平洋近海地震發生時，晴空塔已接近完成高度，天線塔仍在頂升階段；地震後塔體接受全面檢查，業主公開表示人員安全、結構無損，一週後的 3 月 18 日達到 634 m。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When the Tōhoku earthquake struck on 11 March 2011, Skytree was close to full height with the antenna mast still being lifted; the tower was fully inspected afterwards, the owner announced that workers were safe and the structure undamaged, and it reached 634 m a week later on 18 March. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b024-v13-30","title":"2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查：定量估算","titleEn":"Inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「施工中強震後檢查」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Post-earthquake inspection during construction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：殘留傾斜判斷：比較地震前後同一時段、相近溫度下的頂部座標，若差值 12 mm、量測高度 600 m，傾角 12/600,000 = 1/50,000；若量測不確定度為 ±15 mm，差值小於兩倍不確定度，可判定沒有可量測的殘留變形。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Residual tilt check: compare top coordinates before and after the earthquake at the same time of day and similar temperature; a 12 mm difference at 600 m is a tilt of 12/600,000 = 1/50,000, and with a survey uncertainty of ±15 mm the change is below twice the uncertainty, so no measurable residual deformation is concluded. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依事先訂好的地震後檢查清單，優先檢查臨時支承、頂升設備、已安裝阻尼器與高應力接頭，以目視、超音波與螺栓扭力抽查；同時比對地震前後的測量資料與現場加速度紀錄，確認結構反應在施工階段分析的預期範圍內，才恢復作業。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Follow a pre-agreed post-earthquake checklist, inspecting temporary supports, lifting equipment, installed dampers and highly stressed connections first by visual, ultrasonic and bolt-torque checks; compare pre- and post-earthquake survey data and site acceleration records to confirm the response was within the construction-stage analysis predictions before work resumes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"殘留傾斜判斷：比較地震前後同一時段、相近溫度下的頂部座標，若差值 12 mm、量測高度 600 m，傾角 12/600,000 = 1/50,000；若量測不確定度為 ±15 mm，差值小於兩倍不確定度，可判定沒有可量測的殘留變形。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Residual tilt check: compare top coordinates before and after the earthquake at the same time of day and similar temperature; a 12 mm difference at 600 m is a tilt of 12/600,000 = 1/50,000, and with a survey uncertainty of ±15 mm the change is below twice the uncertainty, so no measurable residual deformation is concluded. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake\", which statement holds?","options":["殘留傾斜判斷：比較地震前後同一時段、相近溫度下的頂部座標，若差值 12 mm、量測高度 600 m，傾角 12/600,000 = 1/50,000。","格構塔透風，所以風力可以忽略。","鋼管越粗越厚就越安全，接頭細節不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Residual tilt check: compare top coordinates before and after the earthquake at the same time of day and similar temperature.","A lattice tower lets the wind through, so wind force can be ignored.","The bigger and thicker the tube, the safer it is; joint details do not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"殘留傾斜判斷：比較地震前後同一時段、相近溫度下的頂部座標，若差值 12 mm、量測高度 600 m，傾角 12/600,000 = 1/50,000；若量測不確定度為 ±15 mm，差值小於兩倍不確定度，可判定沒有可量測的殘留變形。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Residual tilt check: compare top coordinates before and after the earthquake at the same time of day and similar temperature; a 12 mm difference at 600 m is a tilt of 12/600,000 = 1/50,000, and with a survey uncertainty of ±15 mm the change is below twice the uncertainty, so no measurable residual deformation is concluded. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b024-v13-31","title":"2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「施工中強震後檢查」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post-earthquake inspection during construction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依事先訂好的地震後檢查清單，優先檢查臨時支承、頂升設備、已安裝阻尼器與高應力接頭，以目視、超音波與螺栓扭力抽查；同時比對地震前後的測量資料與現場加速度紀錄，確認結構反應在施工階段分析的預期範圍內，才恢復作業。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Follow a pre-agreed post-earthquake checklist, inspecting temporary supports, lifting equipment, installed dampers and highly stressed connections first by visual, ultrasonic and bolt-torque checks; compare pre- and post-earthquake survey data and site acceleration records to confirm the response was within the construction-stage analysis predictions before work resumes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工計畫中要預先寫好地震後的停工門檻（例如現場加速度超過設定值）、檢查清單、負責技師與復工簽認程序，並定期保存基準測量資料，以便事件後立即比對。","observationEn":"Site practice: Write post-earthquake stop thresholds such as a site acceleration above a set value, a checklist, the responsible engineer and the restart sign-off procedure into the construction plan in advance, and keep baseline surveys up to date for immediate comparison after an event.","failure":"注意干擾：若只以完工設計檢核地震影響，可能忽略施工中缺少阻尼與臨時支承較弱的狀態，損傷藏在臨時接頭或頂升導引中；沒有地震前的基準測量，事後也無法判斷是否產生殘留變形。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assessing earthquake effects only against the completed design can overlook the construction state with missing damping and weaker temporary supports, leaving damage hidden in temporary connections or lifting guides; without a pre-earthquake baseline survey, residual deformation cannot be judged afterwards. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依事先訂好的地震後檢查清單，優先檢查臨時支承、頂升設備、已安裝阻尼器與高應力接頭，以目視、超音波與螺栓扭力抽查；同時比對地震前後的測量資料與現場加速度紀錄，確認結構反應在施工階段分析的預期範圍內，才恢復作業。","textEn":"Follow a pre-agreed post-earthquake checklist, inspecting temporary supports, lifting equipment, installed dampers and highly stressed connections first by visual, ultrasonic and bolt-torque checks; compare pre- and post-earthquake survey data and site acceleration records to confirm the response was within the construction-stage analysis predictions before work resumes.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工計畫中要預先寫好地震後的停工門檻（例如現場加速度超過設定值）、檢查清單、負責技師與復工簽認程序，並定期保存基準測量資料，以便事件後立即比對。","textEn":"Write post-earthquake stop thresholds such as a site acceleration above a set value, a checklist, the responsible engineer and the restart sign-off procedure into the construction plan in advance, and keep baseline surveys up to date for immediate comparison after an event.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","依事先訂好的地震後檢查清單，優先檢查臨時支承、頂升設備、已安裝阻尼器與高應力接頭，以目視、超音波與螺栓扭力抽查。","鋼構安裝只要每段都對準設計座標，量測時間不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Follow a pre-agreed post-earthquake checklist, inspecting temporary supports, lifting equipment, installed dampers and highly stressed connections first by visual, ultrasonic and bolt-torque checks.","As long as each segment is set to design coordinates, the time of surveying does not matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"依事先訂好的地震後檢查清單，優先檢查臨時支承、頂升設備、已安裝阻尼器與高應力接頭，以目視、超音波與螺栓扭力抽查；同時比對地震前後的測量資料與現場加速度紀錄，確認結構反應在施工階段分析的預期範圍內，才恢復作業。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Follow a pre-agreed post-earthquake checklist, inspecting temporary supports, lifting equipment, installed dampers and highly stressed connections first by visual, ultrasonic and bolt-torque checks; compare pre- and post-earthquake survey data and site acceleration records to confirm the response was within the construction-stage analysis predictions before work resumes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b024-v13-32","title":"2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查：失效診斷","titleEn":"Inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「施工中強震後檢查」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post-earthquake inspection during construction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只以完工設計檢核地震影響，可能忽略施工中缺少阻尼與臨時支承較弱的狀態，損傷藏在臨時接頭或頂升導引中；沒有地震前的基準測量，事後也無法判斷是否產生殘留變形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assessing earthquake effects only against the completed design can overlook the construction state with missing damping and weaker temporary supports, leaving damage hidden in temporary connections or lifting guides; without a pre-earthquake baseline survey, residual deformation cannot be judged afterwards. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：施工中的結構與完工狀態不同：阻尼器可能尚未全部連接、臨時支承仍在、上部有移動中的構件，因此地震後的檢查必須以當時的施工狀態為基準，而不是以完工設計為基準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A structure under construction differs from the finished state: dampers may not all be connected, temporary supports remain and members at the top may be in motion, so post-earthquake inspection must be based on the construction state at the time, not on the completed design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地震後只要外觀沒有明顯損壞，施工中的結構就可以立即復工。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If there is no visible damage after an earthquake, work on an unfinished structure can resume immediately.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只以完工設計檢核地震影響，可能忽略施工中缺少阻尼與臨時支承較弱的狀態，損傷藏在臨時接頭或頂升導引中；沒有地震前的基準測量，事後也無法判斷是否產生殘留變形。","textEn":"Assessing earthquake effects only against the completed design can overlook the construction state with missing damping and weaker temporary supports, leaving damage hidden in temporary connections or lifting guides; without a pre-earthquake baseline survey, residual deformation cannot be judged afterwards.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「2011 年地震時施工中塔體的檢查」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Inspecting the unfinished tower after the 2011 earthquake\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","落冰只是維護清潔問題，和結構工程無關。","若只以完工設計檢核地震影響，可能忽略施工中缺少阻尼與臨時支承較弱的狀態，損傷藏在臨時接頭或頂升導引中；沒有地震前的基準測量，事後也無法判斷是否產生殘留變形。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Falling ice is only a cleaning issue and has nothing to do with structural engineering.","Assessing earthquake effects only against the completed design can overlook the construction state with missing damping and weaker temporary supports, leaving damage hidden in temporary connections or lifting guides."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若只以完工設計檢核地震影響，可能忽略施工中缺少阻尼與臨時支承較弱的狀態，損傷藏在臨時接頭或頂升導引中；沒有地震前的基準測量，事後也無法判斷是否產生殘留變形。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assessing earthquake effects only against the completed design can overlook the construction state with missing damping and weaker temporary supports, leaving damage hidden in temporary connections or lifting guides; without a pre-earthquake baseline survey, residual deformation cannot be judged afterwards. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b024-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「高聳塔體的結冰、落冰與周邊防護」與「鋼管塔的防蝕塗裝與長期維護」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Icing, ice fall and perimeter protection on a tall tower\" and \"Coating and long-term upkeep of a tubular steel tower\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b024-v13-33","title":"高聳塔體的結冰、落冰與周邊防護：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Icing, ice fall and perimeter protection on a tall tower: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「冬季結冰與落冰」如何影響東京晴空塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Winter icing and ice fall” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tokyo Skytree”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"晴空塔在 2012 年 2 月完工前後與 2013 年 1 月，曾有雪與冰塊從塔身掉落，損壞鄰近倉庫屋頂並打穿民宅屋頂，成為營運上的結構安全議題。高空溫度低、風大，雪與冰會附著在鋼管與平台上，氣溫回升或強風時成片剝落，從數百公尺高處落下。冰塊的危險取決於其質量與終端速度：較大的冰塊受空氣阻力的影響較小，落地時速度與能量都很高，足以穿透屋頂。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「冬季結冰與落冰」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In February 2012, around completion, and again in January 2013, snow and ice fell from Skytree, damaging nearby warehouse roofs and holing a house roof, making ice an operational structural-safety issue. At height it is cold and windy, so snow and ice cling to tubes and platforms and shed in sheets when temperatures rise or wind strengthens, falling from hundreds of metres. The hazard depends on the ice's mass and terminal velocity: larger pieces are less slowed by air drag and land with high speed and energy, enough to penetrate a roof. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Winter icing and ice fall” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：終端速度 v_t = √(2mg/(ρ·C_d·A))。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Terminal velocity v_t = √(2mg/(ρ·C_d·A)).","failure":"常見誤解：「落冰只是維護清潔問題，和結構工程無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Falling ice is only a cleaning issue and has nothing to do with structural engineering.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「冬季結冰與落冰」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Winter icing and ice fall”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-33-k1","title":"高聳塔體的結冰、落冰與周邊防護","titleEn":"Icing, ice fall and perimeter protection on a tall tower","text":"晴空塔在 2012 年 2 月完工前後與 2013 年 1 月，曾有雪與冰塊從塔身掉落，損壞鄰近倉庫屋頂並打穿民宅屋頂，成為營運上的結構安全議題。高空溫度低、風大，雪與冰會附著在鋼管與平台上，氣溫回升或強風時成片剝落，從數百公尺高處落下。","textEn":"In February 2012, around completion, and again in January 2013, snow and ice fell from Skytree, damaging nearby warehouse roofs and holing a house roof, making ice an operational structural-safety issue. At height it is cold and windy, so snow and ice cling to tubes and platforms and shed in sheets when temperatures rise or wind strengthens, falling from hundreds of metres.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：落冰只是維護清潔問題，和結構工程無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Falling ice is only a cleaning issue and has nothing to do with structural engineering. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高聳塔體的結冰、落冰與周邊防護」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Icing, ice fall and perimeter protection on a tall tower\" is correct?","options":["晴空塔在 2012 年 2 月完工前後與 2013 年 1 月，曾有雪與冰塊從塔身掉落，損壞鄰近倉庫屋頂並打穿民宅屋頂，成為營運上的結構安全議題。","落冰只是維護清潔問題，和結構工程無關。","主鋼管很厚，所以腐蝕對鋼管塔沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["In February 2012, around completion, and again in January 2013, snow and ice fell from Skytree, damaging nearby warehouse roofs and holing a house roof, making ice an operational structural-safety issue.","Falling ice is only a cleaning issue and has nothing to do with structural engineering.","The main tubes are very thick, so corrosion does not matter for a tube tower."],"answer":0,"explanation":"晴空塔在 2012 年 2 月完工前後與 2013 年 1 月，曾有雪與冰塊從塔身掉落，損壞鄰近倉庫屋頂並打穿民宅屋頂，成為營運上的結構安全議題。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In February 2012, around completion, and again in January 2013, snow and ice fell from Skytree, damaging nearby warehouse roofs and holing a house roof, making ice an operational structural-safety issue. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b024-v13-34","title":"高聳塔體的結冰、落冰與周邊防護：定量估算","titleEn":"Icing, ice fall and perimeter protection on a tall tower: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「冬季結冰與落冰」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Winter icing and ice fall” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：終端速度 v_t = √(2mg/(ρ·C_d·A))。冰塊 m = 2 kg、迎風面積 A = 0.02 m²、C_d = 1.0：v_t = √(2×2×9.81/(1.225×1.0×0.02)) ≈ 40 m/s，動能 ½·m·v² ≈ 0.5×2×40² = 1,600 J；若無空氣阻力，自 300 m 落下速度約 77 m/s。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Terminal velocity v_t = √(2mg/(ρ·C_d·A)). For a 2 kg piece of ice with A = 0.02 m² and C_d = 1.0, v_t = √(2×2×9.81/(1.225×1.0×0.02)) ≈ 40 m/s and its kinetic energy is ½·m·v² ≈ 0.5×2×40² = 1,600 J; without drag it would reach about 77 m/s after falling 300 m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以氣象資料與現場觀測記錄結冰高度、厚度與剝落時機，配合風向推估落冰範圍並繪製危險區地圖；檢查周邊屋頂與遮棚的抗衝擊能力，並在降雪後巡檢塔身易積冰部位，必要時以融雪或除冰設施處理。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record icing height, thickness and shedding timing from weather data and site observation, estimate the fall zone with wind direction to map hazard areas, check the impact resistance of nearby roofs and canopies, and inspect ice-prone parts of the tower after snowfall, using snow-melting or de-icing measures where needed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"終端速度 v_t = √(2mg/(ρ·C_d·A))。冰塊 m = 2 kg、迎風面積 A = 0.02 m²、C_d = 1.0：v_t = √(2×2×9.81/(1.225×1.0×0.02)) ≈ 40 m/s，動能 ½·m·v² ≈ 0.5×2×40² = 1,600 J；若無空氣阻力，自 300 m 落下速度約 77 m/s。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Terminal velocity v_t = √(2mg/(ρ·C_d·A)). For a 2 kg piece of ice with A = 0.02 m² and C_d = 1.0, v_t = √(2×2×9.81/(1.225×1.0×0.02)) ≈ 40 m/s and its kinetic energy is ½·m·v² ≈ 0.5×2×40² = 1,600 J; without drag it would reach about 77 m/s after falling 300 m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高聳塔體的結冰、落冰與周邊防護」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Icing, ice fall and perimeter protection on a tall tower\", which statement holds?","options":["心柱是用來支撐鋼塔重量的主柱。","終端速度 v_t = √(2mg/(ρ·C_d·A))。","塔很重，所以基礎只需要考慮下壓，不會受拉。"],"optionsEn":["The central column is the main column that carries the steel tower's weight.","Terminal velocity v_t = √(2mg/(ρ·C_d·A)).","The tower is heavy, so its foundation only needs to resist compression and never tension."],"answer":1,"explanation":"終端速度 v_t = √(2mg/(ρ·C_d·A))。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Terminal velocity v_t = √(2mg/(ρ·C_d·A)). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b024-v13-35","title":"高聳塔體的結冰、落冰與周邊防護：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Icing, ice fall and perimeter protection on a tall tower: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「冬季結冰與落冰」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Winter icing and ice fall” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以氣象資料與現場觀測記錄結冰高度、厚度與剝落時機，配合風向推估落冰範圍並繪製危險區地圖；檢查周邊屋頂與遮棚的抗衝擊能力，並在降雪後巡檢塔身易積冰部位，必要時以融雪或除冰設施處理。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record icing height, thickness and shedding timing from weather data and site observation, estimate the fall zone with wind direction to map hazard areas, check the impact resistance of nearby roofs and canopies, and inspect ice-prone parts of the tower after snowfall, using snow-melting or de-icing measures where needed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：營運手冊要包含結冰預警條件、周邊管制區範圍、遮棚與屋頂防護規格，以及降雪後的巡檢路線；每次落冰事件都記錄位置與冰塊大小，回饋給結構與設施管理單位修正防護範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: The operations manual should include icing warning conditions, the exclusion zone, specifications for canopies and roof protection, and post-snowfall inspection routes; record the location and size of every ice-fall event and feed it back to the structural and facilities teams to adjust the protected area.","failure":"注意干擾：若沒有落冰預警與管制，冰塊可能擊中行人或車輛，造成人命傷亡與第三人損害；長期附冰也會增加構件重量與受風面積，並在融化再凍結時讓水滲入接縫，加速腐蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without ice-fall warnings and controls, ice can strike pedestrians or vehicles, causing injuries and third-party damage; long-term icing also adds weight and wind area to members and lets meltwater refreeze in joints, accelerating corrosion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以氣象資料與現場觀測記錄結冰高度、厚度與剝落時機，配合風向推估落冰範圍並繪製危險區地圖；檢查周邊屋頂與遮棚的抗衝擊能力，並在降雪後巡檢塔身易積冰部位，必要時以融雪或除冰設施處理。","textEn":"Record icing height, thickness and shedding timing from weather data and site observation, estimate the fall zone with wind direction to map hazard areas, check the impact resistance of nearby roofs and canopies, and inspect ice-prone parts of the tower after snowfall, using snow-melting or de-icing measures where needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"營運手冊要包含結冰預警條件、周邊管制區範圍、遮棚與屋頂防護規格，以及降雪後的巡檢路線；每次落冰事件都記錄位置與冰塊大小，回饋給結構與設施管理單位修正防護範圍。","textEn":"The operations manual should include icing warning conditions, the exclusion zone, specifications for canopies and roof protection, and post-snowfall inspection routes; record the location and size of every ice-fall event and feed it back to the structural and facilities teams to adjust the protected area.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高聳塔體的結冰、落冰與周邊防護」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Icing, ice fall and perimeter protection on a tall tower\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","在豎井內頂升比較安全，所以不需要另做結構分析。","以氣象資料與現場觀測記錄結冰高度、厚度與剝落時機，配合風向推估落冰範圍並繪製危險區地圖。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Lifting inside the shaft is safer, so no separate structural analysis is needed.","Record icing height, thickness and shedding timing from weather data and site observation, estimate the fall zone with wind direction to map hazard areas, check the impact resistance of nearby roofs and canopies, and inspect ice-prone parts of the tower after snowfall, using snow-melting or de-icing measures where needed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以氣象資料與現場觀測記錄結冰高度、厚度與剝落時機，配合風向推估落冰範圍並繪製危險區地圖；檢查周邊屋頂與遮棚的抗衝擊能力，並在降雪後巡檢塔身易積冰部位，必要時以融雪或除冰設施處理。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record icing height, thickness and shedding timing from weather data and site observation, estimate the fall zone with wind direction to map hazard areas, check the impact resistance of nearby roofs and canopies, and inspect ice-prone parts of the tower after snowfall, using snow-melting or de-icing measures where needed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b024-v13-36","title":"高聳塔體的結冰、落冰與周邊防護：失效診斷","titleEn":"Icing, ice fall and perimeter protection on a tall tower: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「冬季結冰與落冰」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Winter icing and ice fall” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若沒有落冰預警與管制，冰塊可能擊中行人或車輛，造成人命傷亡與第三人損害；長期附冰也會增加構件重量與受風面積，並在融化再凍結時讓水滲入接縫，加速腐蝕。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without ice-fall warnings and controls, ice can strike pedestrians or vehicles, causing injuries and third-party damage; long-term icing also adds weight and wind area to members and lets meltwater refreeze in joints, accelerating corrosion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：冰塊的危險取決於其質量與終端速度：較大的冰塊受空氣阻力的影響較小，落地時速度與能量都很高，足以穿透屋頂。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The hazard depends on the ice's mass and terminal velocity: larger pieces are less slowed by air drag and land with high speed and energy, enough to penetrate a roof.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「落冰只是維護清潔問題，和結構工程無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Falling ice is only a cleaning issue and has nothing to do with structural engineering.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若沒有落冰預警與管制，冰塊可能擊中行人或車輛，造成人命傷亡與第三人損害；長期附冰也會增加構件重量與受風面積，並在融化再凍結時讓水滲入接縫，加速腐蝕。","textEn":"Without ice-fall warnings and controls, ice can strike pedestrians or vehicles, causing injuries and third-party damage; long-term icing also adds weight and wind area to members and lets meltwater refreeze in joints, accelerating corrosion.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高聳塔體的結冰、落冰與周邊防護」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Icing, ice fall and perimeter protection on a tall tower\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若沒有落冰預警與管制，冰塊可能擊中行人或車輛，造成人命傷亡與第三人損害；長期附冰也會增加構件重量與受風面積，並在融化再凍結時讓水滲入接縫，加速腐蝕。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","主鋼管很厚，所以腐蝕對鋼管塔沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Without ice-fall warnings and controls, ice can strike pedestrians or vehicles, causing injuries and third-party damage.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The main tubes are very thick, so corrosion does not matter for a tube tower."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若沒有落冰預警與管制，冰塊可能擊中行人或車輛，造成人命傷亡與第三人損害；長期附冰也會增加構件重量與受風面積，並在融化再凍結時讓水滲入接縫，加速腐蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without ice-fall warnings and controls, ice can strike pedestrians or vehicles, causing injuries and third-party damage; long-term icing also adds weight and wind area to members and lets meltwater refreeze in joints, accelerating corrosion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b024-v13-37","title":"鋼管塔的防蝕塗裝與長期維護：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Coating and long-term upkeep of a tubular steel tower: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「鋼管塔防蝕塗裝」如何影響東京晴空塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Corrosion coating of the tube tower” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tokyo Skytree”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"晴空塔的鋼構塗以名為「SKYTREE White」的原創顏色，以傳統藍染中最淡的「藍白」為基調，在白色中加入淡淡的藍。對結構工程師而言，塗裝不只是外觀，而是鋼構防蝕的第一道防線；634 m 的格構塔有大量相貫接頭、平台與排水死角，雨水與結露容易積在接頭與構件交會處。圓管外表面容易塗裝，但封閉的管內必須確實密封或另做防蝕，否則內部腐蝕無法目視發現。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鋼管塔防蝕塗裝」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Skytree's steelwork is painted in an original colour called SKYTREE White, based on aijiro, the palest shade of traditional indigo dyeing, with a faint blue added to white. For the structural engineer the coating is not just appearance but the first line of corrosion protection; a 634 m lattice tower has many intersecting joints, platforms and drainage dead spots where rain and condensation collect. The outside of a round tube is easy to coat, but the inside of a closed tube must be reliably sealed or separately protected, otherwise internal corrosion cannot be seen. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Corrosion coating of the tube tower” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：鋼材腐蝕損失 = 年腐蝕率 × 年數。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Section loss = annual corrosion rate × years.","failure":"常見誤解：「主鋼管很厚，所以腐蝕對鋼管塔沒有影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The main tubes are very thick, so corrosion does not matter for a tube tower.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鋼管塔防蝕塗裝」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Corrosion coating of the tube tower”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-37-k1","title":"鋼管塔的防蝕塗裝與長期維護","titleEn":"Coating and long-term upkeep of a tubular steel tower","text":"晴空塔的鋼構塗以名為「SKYTREE White」的原創顏色，以傳統藍染中最淡的「藍白」為基調，在白色中加入淡淡的藍。對結構工程師而言，塗裝不只是外觀，而是鋼構防蝕的第一道防線；634 m 的格構塔有大量相貫接頭、平台與排水死角，雨水與結露容易積在接頭與構件交會處。","textEn":"Skytree's steelwork is painted in an original colour called SKYTREE White, based on aijiro, the palest shade of traditional indigo dyeing, with a faint blue added to white. For the structural engineer the coating is not just appearance but the first line of corrosion protection; a 634 m lattice tower has many intersecting joints, platforms and drainage dead spots where rain and condensation collect.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：主鋼管很厚，所以腐蝕對鋼管塔沒有影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The main tubes are very thick, so corrosion does not matter for a tube tower. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼管塔的防蝕塗裝與長期維護」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Coating and long-term upkeep of a tubular steel tower\" is correct?","options":["主鋼管很厚，所以腐蝕對鋼管塔沒有影響。","晴空塔的鋼構塗以名為「SKYTREE White」的原創顏色，以傳統藍染中最淡的「藍白」為基調，在白色中加入淡淡的藍。","格構塔透風，所以風力可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["The main tubes are very thick, so corrosion does not matter for a tube tower.","Skytree's steelwork is painted in an original colour called SKYTREE White, based on aijiro, the palest shade of traditional indigo dyeing, with a faint blue added to white.","A lattice tower lets the wind through, so wind force can be ignored."],"answer":1,"explanation":"晴空塔的鋼構塗以名為「SKYTREE White」的原創顏色，以傳統藍染中最淡的「藍白」為基調，在白色中加入淡淡的藍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Skytree's steelwork is painted in an original colour called SKYTREE White, based on aijiro, the palest shade of traditional indigo dyeing, with a faint blue added to white. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b024-v13-38","title":"鋼管塔的防蝕塗裝與長期維護：定量估算","titleEn":"Coating and long-term upkeep of a tubular steel tower: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼管塔防蝕塗裝」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Corrosion coating of the tube tower” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：鋼材腐蝕損失 = 年腐蝕率 × 年數。若塗膜失效後裸鋼以 0.03 mm/年腐蝕，30 年單面損失約 0.9 mm；對 100 mm 厚的主管影響不到 1%，但 12 mm 厚的節點板兩面腐蝕共 1.8 mm，斷面損失達 15%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Section loss = annual corrosion rate × years. If bare steel corrodes at 0.03 mm per year after the coating fails, 30 years remove about 0.9 mm per face; that is under 1% of a 100 mm main tube but, on a 12 mm gusset corroding on both faces, 1.8 mm or 15% of the section. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：定期以膜厚計、附著力試驗與目視分級檢查塗膜，優先抽查相貫接頭、平台積水處與高空不易到達的部位；封閉鋼管以內部濕度監測或抽樣開孔檢查確認密封有效，結果寫入以構件編號管理的維護資料庫。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Inspect coatings periodically with film-thickness gauges, adhesion tests and visual grading, prioritising intersecting joints, ponding spots on platforms and hard-to-reach high areas; confirm closed tubes are still sealed by internal humidity monitoring or sample inspection openings, recording results in a maintenance database indexed by member number.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"鋼材腐蝕損失 = 年腐蝕率 × 年數。若塗膜失效後裸鋼以 0.03 mm/年腐蝕，30 年單面損失約 0.9 mm；對 100 mm 厚的主管影響不到 1%，但 12 mm 厚的節點板兩面腐蝕共 1.8 mm，斷面損失達 15%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Section loss = annual corrosion rate × years. If bare steel corrodes at 0.03 mm per year after the coating fails, 30 years remove about 0.9 mm per face; that is under 1% of a 100 mm main tube but, on a 12 mm gusset corroding on both faces, 1.8 mm or 15% of the section. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼管塔的防蝕塗裝與長期維護」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Coating and long-term upkeep of a tubular steel tower\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼管越粗越厚就越安全，接頭細節不重要。","鋼構安裝只要每段都對準設計座標，量測時間不重要。","鋼材腐蝕損失 = 年腐蝕率 × 年數。"],"optionsEn":["The bigger and thicker the tube, the safer it is; joint details do not matter.","As long as each segment is set to design coordinates, the time of surveying does not matter.","Section loss = annual corrosion rate × years."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鋼材腐蝕損失 = 年腐蝕率 × 年數。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Section loss = annual corrosion rate × years. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b024-v13-39","title":"鋼管塔的防蝕塗裝與長期維護：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Coating and long-term upkeep of a tubular steel tower: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼管塔防蝕塗裝」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Corrosion coating of the tube tower” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"定期以膜厚計、附著力試驗與目視分級檢查塗膜，優先抽查相貫接頭、平台積水處與高空不易到達的部位；封閉鋼管以內部濕度監測或抽樣開孔檢查確認密封有效，結果寫入以構件編號管理的維護資料庫。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Inspect coatings periodically with film-thickness gauges, adhesion tests and visual grading, prioritising intersecting joints, ponding spots on platforms and hard-to-reach high areas; confirm closed tubes are still sealed by internal humidity monitoring or sample inspection openings, recording results in a maintenance database indexed by member number. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件要包含塗裝系統規格、顏色配方、各部位膜厚紀錄、檢查週期與高空作業通道圖；維護計畫依部位分級訂出檢查頻率，薄構件與接頭列為最高優先，並編列定期重塗的經費與時程。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover documents include the coating specification, colour formula, film-thickness records by location, inspection intervals and high-access routes; the maintenance plan grades locations by inspection frequency, puts thin members and joints at highest priority, and budgets and schedules periodic recoating.","failure":"注意干擾：若只在容易到達的低處補漆，高處接頭與平台下方的腐蝕可能持續數十年未被發現；薄節點板與螺栓先腐蝕變薄，會成為整座塔的弱點，而主管看起來仍完好。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Touching up only easily reached low areas can leave corrosion at high joints and under platforms undetected for decades; thin gussets and bolts thin first and become the tower's weak points while the main tubes still look sound. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"定期以膜厚計、附著力試驗與目視分級檢查塗膜，優先抽查相貫接頭、平台積水處與高空不易到達的部位；封閉鋼管以內部濕度監測或抽樣開孔檢查確認密封有效，結果寫入以構件編號管理的維護資料庫。","textEn":"Inspect coatings periodically with film-thickness gauges, adhesion tests and visual grading, prioritising intersecting joints, ponding spots on platforms and hard-to-reach high areas; confirm closed tubes are still sealed by internal humidity monitoring or sample inspection openings, recording results in a maintenance database indexed by member number.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件要包含塗裝系統規格、顏色配方、各部位膜厚紀錄、檢查週期與高空作業通道圖；維護計畫依部位分級訂出檢查頻率，薄構件與接頭列為最高優先，並編列定期重塗的經費與時程。","textEn":"Handover documents include the coating specification, colour formula, film-thickness records by location, inspection intervals and high-access routes; the maintenance plan grades locations by inspection frequency, puts thin members and joints at highest priority, and budgets and schedules periodic recoating.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼管塔的防蝕塗裝與長期維護」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Coating and long-term upkeep of a tubular steel tower\"?","options":["定期以膜厚計、附著力試驗與目視分級檢查塗膜，優先抽查相貫接頭、平台積水處與高空不易到達的部位。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","阻尼器的力量越大越好，不需要限制。"],"optionsEn":["Inspect coatings periodically with film-thickness gauges, adhesion tests and visual grading, prioritising intersecting joints, ponding spots on platforms and hard-to-reach high areas.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The larger a damper's force the better, so it needs no limit."],"answer":0,"explanation":"定期以膜厚計、附著力試驗與目視分級檢查塗膜，優先抽查相貫接頭、平台積水處與高空不易到達的部位；封閉鋼管以內部濕度監測或抽樣開孔檢查確認密封有效，結果寫入以構件編號管理的維護資料庫。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Inspect coatings periodically with film-thickness gauges, adhesion tests and visual grading, prioritising intersecting joints, ponding spots on platforms and hard-to-reach high areas; confirm closed tubes are still sealed by internal humidity monitoring or sample inspection openings, recording results in a maintenance database indexed by member number. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b024-v13-40","title":"鋼管塔的防蝕塗裝與長期維護：失效診斷","titleEn":"Coating and long-term upkeep of a tubular steel tower: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"prerequisiteIds":["b024-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼管塔防蝕塗裝」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Corrosion coating of the tube tower” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只在容易到達的低處補漆，高處接頭與平台下方的腐蝕可能持續數十年未被發現；薄節點板與螺栓先腐蝕變薄，會成為整座塔的弱點，而主管看起來仍完好。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Touching up only easily reached low areas can leave corrosion at high joints and under platforms undetected for decades; thin gussets and bolts thin first and become the tower's weak points while the main tubes still look sound. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓管外表面容易塗裝，但封閉的管內必須確實密封或另做防蝕，否則內部腐蝕無法目視發現。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The outside of a round tube is easy to coat, but the inside of a closed tube must be reliably sealed or separately protected, otherwise internal corrosion cannot be seen.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「主鋼管很厚，所以腐蝕對鋼管塔沒有影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The main tubes are very thick, so corrosion does not matter for a tube tower.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b024-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只在容易到達的低處補漆，高處接頭與平台下方的腐蝕可能持續數十年未被發現；薄節點板與螺栓先腐蝕變薄，會成為整座塔的弱點，而主管看起來仍完好。","textEn":"Touching up only easily reached low areas can leave corrosion at high joints and under platforms undetected for decades; thin gussets and bolts thin first and become the tower's weak points while the main tubes still look sound.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]},{"id":"b024-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼管塔的防蝕塗裝與長期維護」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Coating and long-term upkeep of a tubular steel tower\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若只在容易到達的低處補漆，高處接頭與平台下方的腐蝕可能持續數十年未被發現；薄節點板與螺栓先腐蝕變薄，會成為整座塔的弱點，而主管看起來仍完好。","格構塔透風，所以風力可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Touching up only easily reached low areas can leave corrosion at high joints and under platforms undetected for decades.","A lattice tower lets the wind through, so wind force can be ignored."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只在容易到達的低處補漆，高處接頭與平台下方的腐蝕可能持續數十年未被發現；薄節點板與螺栓先腐蝕變薄，會成為整座塔的弱點，而主管看起來仍完好。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Touching up only easily reached low areas can leave corrosion at high joints and under platforms undetected for decades; thin gussets and bolts thin first and become the tower's weak points while the main tubes still look sound. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-skytree-official-spec","v13s-skytree-official-design","v13s-wcn-tokyo-sky-tree","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-en","v13s-wiki-tokyo-skytree-ja"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
